    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/search.atom?utf8=%E2%9C%93&query=&query_v0_posted_at_date=&query_position_type_id%5B%5D=2&435=&commit=Search": {
      "title": "Texas State University-San Marcos : All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:jobs.hr.txstate.edu,2005:/postings/search Texas State University-San Marcos : All Jobs 2026-09-04T09:54:32-05:00 https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58390 2026-09-04T09:54:29-05:00 2026-09-04T09:54:32-05:00 Residence Director - Multiple Positions <div>The Residence Director position is a full-time, live-in role with primary responsibility for managing the daily operations of one or more residential buildings. Residence Directors (RD) are responsible for building a strong community, supporting staff through supervision, and generating meaningful opportunities for students to connect to campus through intentional interactions and connections. Critical functions of the position include building management, supervision, community engagement, crisis management, and student success while serving as an active department member. This position will report directly to an Assistant Director of Residential Experience. The RD must be able to physically perform the job’s essential duties, which include regularly accessing all areas of their assigned residential building and periodically accessing other campus areas. In emergencies, the RD must be able to access all various building areas promptly and appropriately. The Residence Director (RD) will frequently utilize a computer and a phone.</div> DHRL Administration <ul><li>Bachelor’s degree.</li><li>Post bachelor experience in Student Affairs.</li><li>Served in a defined leadership role in one or more of the following: residence life, student activities and organizations, student government, orientation, or professional experience in a university setting.</li></ul> <ul><li>Master’s degree in Student Affairs or related field.</li><li>Previous experience in building management.</li><li>Previous experience in staff supervision.</li><li>Previous experience in crisis management and/or emergency response.</li><li>Previous experience with community engagement/development activities.</li><li>Previous experience with student support or retention initiatives.</li></ul> <div>The Residence Director position is a full-time, live-in role with primary responsibility for managing the daily operations of one or more residential buildings. Residence Directors (RD) are responsible for building a strong community, supporting staff through supervision, and generating meaningful opportunities for students to connect to campus through intentional interactions and connections. Critical functions of the position include building management, supervision, community engagement, crisis management, and student success while serving as an active department member. This position will report directly to an Assistant Director of Residential Experience. The RD must be able to physically perform the job’s essential duties, which include regularly accessing all areas of their assigned residential building and periodically accessing other campus areas. In emergencies, the RD must be able to access all various building areas promptly and appropriately. The Residence Director (RD) will frequently utilize a computer and a phone.</div> <div><strong>Supervision</strong></div><ul><li>Provide day-to-day supervision and support of a staff of Resident Assistants (RA) and Desk Assistants (DA) within their assigned residential building(s).</li><li>Directly oversee and manage staff-wide meetings, one-on-one meetings, and other interactions with student staff to provide maximum support and direction to execute community goals.</li><li>Evaluate performance of student employees, including ongoing performance management and conduct performance evaluations to support their professional development.</li><li>Participate in selection and training efforts for all staff members.</li></ul><div><strong>Student Success &amp; Community Engagement</strong></div><ul><li>Serve as the primary individual responsible for executing the residential experience through hall programs, community-wide events, athletic events, intentional interactions, and other departmental initiatives.</li><li>Direct, assess, and execute community development, engagement activities, and persistence initiatives per departmental directives to increase student retention and a sense of belonging at Texas State University.</li><li>Develop community initiatives and student leadership opportunities as an advisor of Hall Council and within any assigned Living Learning and/or Theme Community.</li><li>Actively participate in Division of Student Success initiatives regarding mid-semester grade warning outreach, enrollment and registration outreach, residential feedback surveys, and other retention initiatives.</li></ul><div><strong>Crisis Management &amp; Student Support</strong></div><ul><li>Serve as a member of the departmental on-call rotation to provide support to students after hours.</li><li>Actively engage with and seek to resolve issues for students of concern to ensure they are supported.</li><li>Serve as a conduct officer to address behavioral concerns within the assigned residential building(s).</li><li>Consistently be responsive to the needs of the assigned residential building(s) in relation to community trends, student needs, and emergency response. This may include being activated to respond to crises outside of normal business hours.</li><li>Serve as a referral agent for students to resources across the institution.</li></ul><div><strong>Building Management</strong></div><ul><li>Assist with responsibilities for opening, closing, budget management, occupancy management, and desk operations within their community.</li><li>Collaborate and meet regularly with assigned facilities team to manage facilities related needs throughout the assigned residential building(s).</li><li>Oversee room occupancy, resident room change requests, and maintenance of resident and common spaces throughout the academic year.</li><li>Maintain essential office records as outlined by Texas State University.</li></ul><div><strong>Divisional &amp; Departmental Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>Actively participate in departmental programs and projects designed to support the mission and goals of the department, division, and institution.</li><li>Participate actively as a member of the Division of Student Success and serve as a positive role model for students and staff.</li><li>Other duties as required.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58388 2026-09-04T08:02:07-05:00 2026-09-04T08:02:08-05:00 Assistant NCAA Certification Officer <div>The Assistant NCAA Athletics Certification Officer is responsible for assisting the NCAA Athletics Certification Officer in obtaining, evaluating, and documenting the academic credentials in accordance with National Collegiate Athletics Association (NCAA) and conference eligibility rules for approximately 400+ student-athletes.</div> Athletic Certification <ul><li>Experience independently researching materials to compile, develop and summarize for professional reports on a frequent or recurring basis.</li><li>Experience analyzing information, identifying problems, defining alternatives, and developing recommendations for administrators.</li><li>Experience interpreting and applying rules, regulations, and laws regarding student records.</li><li>Evidence of the ability to work independently and as a team member.</li><li>Documented experience communicating orally and in writing with varied stakeholders.</li><li>High School Diploma.</li></ul> <ul><li>Bachelor’s Degree</li><li>Documented experience working with NCAA regulations (Bylaw 14) related to athletic academic eligibility.</li><li>Experience in evaluating and interpreting degree plans and curriculum, preferably utilizing Degree Works degree audit system.</li><li>Experience working in the Banner Student Information System environment.</li><li>Experience working with the NCAA Eligibility Center website and NCAA Academic Portal.</li><li>Experience working with Teamworks.</li><li>Knowledge of Texas State’s undergraduate core curriculum and degree program requirements.</li></ul> <div>The Assistant NCAA Athletics Certification Officer is responsible for assisting the NCAA Athletics Certification Officer in obtaining, evaluating, and documenting the academic credentials in accordance with National Collegiate Athletics Association (NCAA) and conference eligibility rules for approximately 400+ student-athletes.</div> <ul><li><strong>Eligibility Worksheets - </strong>Update and monitor individual SA eligibility worksheets and team eligibility worksheets on a continuous basis. Provide feedback and projections regarding NCAA eligibility to Athletics Academic Center in a timely manner.</li><li><strong>Certify Student-Athletes for Competition</strong> - Review the academic credentials for each SA to determine eligibility status. Assimilate and file appropriate documentation to support certification (i.e. NCAA SA Details Report, transcripts, degree audits, academic progress forms, etc.). Create EDF and submit to Athletics Compliance Office.</li><li><strong>Academic Pre-Evaluations - </strong>Conduct an academic pre-evaluations for prospective student-athletes and provide accurate and timely feedback to the Athletics Compliance Office.</li><li><strong>Academic Performance Program - </strong>Assist the NCAA Certification Officer in updating Compliance Assistant 2.0 with pertinent information for the APP (including APR and GSR) each year. Work cooperatively with Athletics Academic Center staff and the Athletics Compliance staff to ensure information is accurate. Provide feedback for any NCAA responses to information.</li><li><strong>Academic Progress Forms - </strong>Create, distribute, review, compile and file the academic progress forms from the College Advising centers. Follow up with each College Advising center in a timely manner for clarification when needed.</li><li><strong>Full-Time Enrollment Monitoring - </strong>Oversee the monitoring of full-time enrollment of SAs, managers, male practice players and graduate assistants.</li><li><strong>Other Assigned Duties</strong> - Assist the NCAA Athletic Compliance Officer with general office organization and support.</li><li><strong>Professionalism</strong> - Appearance, attendance, punctuality, and office decorum met Registrar’s office and University policies consistently.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58370 2026-09-02T13:56:54-05:00 2026-09-02T13:56:56-05:00 Graphic Designer <div>The Graphic Designer position produces high-quality visual design for print, digital, video, and web to support the Division of Student Success and its programs, services, and initiatives. The role ensures consistent application of university and divisional brand standards across all departments, serving as a key steward of the visual identity and advising departments on effective design practices. The position manages a broad range of projects from concept through delivery, balancing multiple deadlines while aligning all materials with the mission and vision of the Division of Student Success. The Graphic Designer works under the direction of the Director of Marketing and Communications, collaborates closely with campus partners, and will supervise and mentor student workers involved in design, media, and production tasks.</div> VP Student Success <ul><li>Bachelor’s degree in visual design, communication, graphic design, advertising, or a closely related field.</li><li>Demonstrated knowledge of design principles and applications for print and digital media.</li><li>Proficiency with Adobe Creative Suite or comparable design software.</li><li>Knowledge of advertising, branding, and campaign development.</li><li>Strong skills in project and process management, including managing multiple concurrent design requests and deadlines.</li><li>Proficiency with computers and common office and design technologies, including printers, photo and video equipment, and basic UX concepts.</li><li>Effective oral and written communication skills, with the ability to communicate professionally with a diverse range of stakeholders.</li><li>Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to work effectively with both professional staff and student employees.</li></ul> <ul><li>Master’s degree in a related field (e.g., communication, graphic design, advertising, or visual design).</li><li>Experience working in a higher education or student affairs environment.</li><li>Experience supervising student employees or managing small creative teams.</li><li>Experience presenting workshops or trainings on design, media, or marketing topics.</li><li>Familiarity with work request and project management systems, including tracking, prioritization, and reporting.</li><li>Demonstrated ability to align creative work with institutional branding, strategic goals, and assessment data.</li></ul> <div>The Graphic Designer position produces high-quality visual design for print, digital, video, and web to support the Division of Student Success and its programs, services, and initiatives. The role ensures consistent application of university and divisional brand standards across all departments, serving as a key steward of the visual identity and advising departments on effective design practices. The position manages a broad range of projects from concept through delivery, balancing multiple deadlines while aligning all materials with the mission and vision of the Division of Student Success. The Graphic Designer works under the direction of the Director of Marketing and Communications, collaborates closely with campus partners, and will supervise and mentor student workers involved in design, media, and production tasks.</div> <div><strong>Design and Creative Production</strong></div><ul><li>Conceptualize and design visual materials for print, digital, web, and video to support Division of Student Success initiatives.</li><li>Develop concepts and layouts from initial idea through final deliverables, ensuring designs are clear, accessible, and audience-focused.</li><li>Select format, typography, color, imagery, and overall layout, and edits content within designs for clarity and impact.</li><li>Create and maintain templates and reusable assets to streamline production and reduce one-off requests.</li></ul><div><strong>Brand Stewardship and Visual Strategy</strong></div><ul><li>Apply and uphold university and divisional brand standards across all materials to ensure a consistent visual identity.</li><li>Align design projects with the mission, vision, and strategic priorities of the Division of Student Success.</li><li>Recommend appropriate channels and mediums (print, digital, web, social, video) to maximize effectiveness and reach.</li><li>Advise staff on best practices for visual communication, including image use, readability, and inclusive design.</li></ul><div><strong>Collaboration and Consultation</strong></div><ul><li>Collaborate with stakeholders to clarify project goals, audiences, timelines, and deliverables.</li><li>Conduct project intake, communicate status and timelines, and incorporate feedback while maintaining design quality and brand alignment.</li><li>Provide guidance or training on topics such as design basics, branding, and effective use of media and visual assets.</li><li>Build and maintain positive working relationships with staff and student employees to support a collaborative, service-oriented environment.</li></ul><div><strong>Project and Team Management</strong></div><ul><li>Manage multiple concurrent design requests, tracking, prioritizing, and scheduling work according to divisional priorities and deadlines.</li><li>Maintain organized shared repositories of design files, templates, assets, and photography for reference and reuse.</li><li>Provide day-to-day direction and feedback to student workers on design and media projects, ensuring quality and consistency.</li><li>Support special projects and other assigned duties, including event-related design needs and rapid-turnaround requests.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58362 2026-09-02T07:41:00-05:00 2026-09-02T07:41:01-05:00 Digital Media Manager <div>&nbsp;Create, curate, and publish high-quality, relevant, and engaging content (graphics, videos, photos, articles, and posts) across platforms including Facebook, Twitter/X, Instagram, LinkedIn, and YouTube.&nbsp;</div> ALERRT Center <ul><li>5 years of demonstrated professional experience in creating and managing social media initiatives on a variety of social media platforms.</li><li>Excellent knowledge of business account management of all social media channels including Facebook, X, Instagram, LinkedIn, YouTube and more.</li><li>Demonstrated experience with social media data collection and analytics.</li><li>A portfolio of work demonstrates the ability to tell complex stories in relatable terms.</li><li>Proven ability to work on multiple priorities simultaneously.</li><li>Excellent customer service skills.</li></ul> <ul><li>Law Enforcement and first responder experience.</li><li>Social Media video creation experience.</li></ul> <div>&nbsp;Create, curate, and publish high-quality, relevant, and engaging content (graphics, videos, photos, articles, and posts) across platforms including Facebook, Twitter/X, Instagram, LinkedIn, and YouTube.&nbsp;</div> <div>Develop and implement a comprehensive social media strategy aligned with ALERRT's mission, training initiatives, and outreach goals.<br>Create, curate, and publish high-quality, relevant, and engaging content (graphics, videos, photos, articles, and posts) across platforms including Facebook, Twitter/X, Instagram, LinkedIn, and YouTube.<br>Collaborate with ALERRT curriculum and training coordinators, subject matter experts, and university partners to promote upcoming courses, events, success stories, and institutional announcements.<br>Monitor social media trends, tools, and best practices to ensure content remains fresh and impactful.</div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58360 2026-09-01T14:00:59-05:00 2026-09-01T14:01:01-05:00 Accountant I <div>Support Services within the Division of Student Success is seeking a detail-oriented and customer-focused Accountant I to support the financial operations of the University Dining program. This position is responsible for processing, recording, reconciling, auditing, and analyzing financial transactions; preparing financial reports; managing billing activities; monitoring account balances and transaction activity; and ensuring compliance with university policies and applicable regulations. The Accountant I reviews and approves payments, invoices, vouchers, and supporting documentation, assists with purchasing and payment processes, and serves as a key resource for financial inquiries from students, vendors, and campus stakeholders. Working closely with Support Services leadership, Student Business Services, Accounts Payable, and external vendors, this position helps ensure accurate financial reporting, timely billing and collections, and effective stewardship of university resources.</div> Support Services <ul><li>Knowledge of accounting principles, financial reporting, account reconciliation, billing, payment processing, and financial record management.</li><li>Ability to analyze financial data, identify discrepancies, and resolve accounting and transaction-related issues.</li><li>Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, for financial analysis and reporting.</li><li>Strong organizational, time-management, and problem-solving skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines</li><li>Strong verbal and written communication skills and the ability to provide professional customer service to students, faculty, staff, vendors, and external stakeholders.</li><li>Ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures, and regulations while maintaining a high degree of accuracy and attention to detail.</li><li>Ability to perform mathematical calculations and prepare accurate financial reports and documentation.</li></ul> <ul><li>Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or a related field.</li><li>One year of professional accounting, bookkeeping, financial reporting, auditing, or reconciliation experience.</li><li>Experience working in higher education, auxiliary services, dining services, or a comparable business environment.</li><li>Experience with SAP, Banner, or similar financial management systems.</li><li>Advanced Excel skills, including pivot tables, formulas, and financial reporting tools.</li></ul> <div>Support Services within the Division of Student Success is seeking a detail-oriented and customer-focused Accountant I to support the financial operations of the University Dining program. This position is responsible for processing, recording, reconciling, auditing, and analyzing financial transactions; preparing financial reports; managing billing activities; monitoring account balances and transaction activity; and ensuring compliance with university policies and applicable regulations. The Accountant I reviews and approves payments, invoices, vouchers, and supporting documentation, assists with purchasing and payment processes, and serves as a key resource for financial inquiries from students, vendors, and campus stakeholders. Working closely with Support Services leadership, Student Business Services, Accounts Payable, and external vendors, this position helps ensure accurate financial reporting, timely billing and collections, and effective stewardship of university resources.</div> <div><strong>Financial Reporting</strong></div><ul><li>Prepare and analyze monthly, quarterly, and annual financial reports for Dining Services and auxiliary operations in DSS support services.</li><li>Monitor financial performance, identify variances, and provide recommendations to support informed decision-making.</li><li>Assist with budget monitoring, forecasting, and financial planning activities.</li></ul><div><strong>Account Reconciliation and Customer Support</strong></div><ul><li>Reconcile student, departmental, vendor, and auxiliary accounts to ensure accurate financial records.</li><li>Research and resolve account discrepancies, transaction issues, and customer inquiries.</li><li>Provide financial support and customer service to students, vendors, and campus departments.</li></ul><div><strong>Purchasing and Expense Management</strong></div><ul><li>Process purchases and financial transactions in compliance with university policies and procurement procedures.</li><li>Monitor expenditures, maintain supporting documentation, and track operational expenses.</li><li>Assist with work order and expenditure tracking to support departmental operations.</li></ul><div><strong>Billing and Payment Processing</strong></div><ul><li>Process, review, and reconcile billings, payments, invoices, vouchers, and deposits.</li><li>Coordinate with Student Business Services, Accounts Payable, and other university departments to ensure timely collection of revenues and payment of vendors.</li><li>Research and resolve billing and payment discrepancies while maintaining compliance with applicable policies and regulations.</li></ul><div><strong>Other Duties</strong></div><ul><li>Perform other related duties as assigned in support of Dining Services and Support Services operations</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58358 2026-09-01T09:37:17-05:00 2026-09-01T09:37:19-05:00 Immigration Advisor <div>The Immigration Advisor, DSO, provides immigration advising and regulatory support to F-1 students on Pre-Completion OPT, Post-Completion OPT, and STEM OPT, ensuring compliance with SEVP and DHS regulations. The role issues OPT/STEM OPT I-20 recommendations, maintains accurate SEVIS records, monitors employment reporting and eligibility requirements, and advises students and employers on work authorization, status maintenance, and Form I-983 compliance. It also processes OPT/STEM OPT requests, conducts workshops and outreach, and supports institutional compliance with federal immigration regulations. This role reports to the Senior Immigration Advisor.</div> International Affairs <ul><li>Experience advising students in a university context.</li><li>Experience researching and interpreting complex rules and regulations.</li><li>F1 immigration regulations</li><li>Demonstrated effective communication skills with attention to detail.</li><li>Knowledge of the Terra Dotta database</li><li>Effective problem-solving skills.</li><li>Ability to work independently and as a team member.</li><li>Ability to work in a fast pace and complex environment.</li><li>Experience with HE software and platforms such as Microsoft Suite and Dynamic Forms.</li><li>Data management and analytics.</li><li>Must be a US Citizen or Permanent Resident</li></ul> <ul><li>Bachelors Degree</li></ul> <div>The Immigration Advisor, DSO, provides immigration advising and regulatory support to F-1 students on Pre-Completion OPT, Post-Completion OPT, and STEM OPT, ensuring compliance with SEVP and DHS regulations. The role issues OPT/STEM OPT I-20 recommendations, maintains accurate SEVIS records, monitors employment reporting and eligibility requirements, and advises students and employers on work authorization, status maintenance, and Form I-983 compliance. It also processes OPT/STEM OPT requests, conducts workshops and outreach, and supports institutional compliance with federal immigration regulations. This role reports to the Senior Immigration Advisor.</div> <div>• Advise F-1 students on eligibility, application procedures, and timelines for Post-Completion OPT and STEM OPT extensions<br>• Conduct individual and group advising sessions on employment authorization regulations, reporting requirements, and travel considerations<br>• Provide guidance on maintaining lawful F-1 status during post-completion employment periods<br>• Educate students and employers on STEM OPT training plan (Form I-983) requirements<br>• Issue OPT and STEM OPT I-20 recommendations in compliance with DHS and SEVP regulations<br>• Update and maintain accurate student records in SEVIS<br>• Monitor employment reporting, unemployment limits, and validation requirements for OPT/STEM OPT participants<br>• Ensure institutional compliance with federal immigration reporting standards<br>• Review and process OPT and STEM OPT requests, including I-765 support documentation<br>• Verify eligibility and supporting documentation for post-completion work authorization<br>• Track deadlines and ensure timely submission of required SEVIS updates and reports<br>• Coordinate with other DSOs and ISSS staff to maintain workflow efficiency<br>• Communicate with employers regarding STEM OPT training plan requirements and compliance expectations<br>• Collaborate with on-campus departments to support experiential learning pathways<br>• Conduct workshops, orientations, and presentations on OPT/STEM OPT processes<br>• Develop informational materials and digital resources for students and advisors<br>• Stay current on federal immigration policy updates affecting F-1 employment authorization<br>• Participate in orientation programs, workshops, and informational sessions to help international students understand and comply with immigration rules and regulations.</div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58332 2026-08-28T11:03:48-05:00 2026-08-28T11:03:50-05:00 Education Mobility Outreach Coordinator <div>The Education Mobility Outreach Coordinator is responsible for providing outreach and recruitment efforts for the three Education Mobility units to increase student enrollment and drive awareness of programs. This position reports directly to the Director of Education Mobility.</div> International Affairs <ul><li>Bachelor’s degree in communications, marketing, higher education, student affairs, international studies, or related field.</li><li>Experience with event planning, outreach, recruitment, communications, or student engagement.</li><li>Excellent interpersonal skills in order to communicate effectively with students, faculty, staff, and community members in 1:1 or presentation style.</li><li>Must be a U.S. citizen to hold certification with the U.S. Department of State as a Passport Facility Agent.</li></ul><div><br></div> <ul><li>Experience working in higher education or student services.</li><li>Experience with international education, study abroad, domestic exchange or student travel, or student mobility programming.</li><li>Experience presenting to groups and coordinating campus events.</li><li>Familiarity with Canva, Adobe Creative Suite, social media analytics, or CRM/student engagement platforms.</li></ul> <div>The Education Mobility Outreach Coordinator is responsible for providing outreach and recruitment efforts for the three Education Mobility units to increase student enrollment and drive awareness of programs. This position reports directly to the Director of Education Mobility.</div> <ul><li>Assist in developing strategies to increase student awareness and participation in Education Abroad and Study in America programs.</li><li>Represent Education Mobility at tabling events, student organization fairs, orientations, classroom presentations, campus events, and community outreach opportunities.</li><li>Conduct presentations and information sessions for students and campus partners. Including, but not limited to, attending New Student Orientations.</li><li>Coordinate logistics and promotional efforts for Education Mobility events, including but not limited to: Education Abroad/Study in America fair, pre-departure orientations, workshops, recruitment events, passport office programing and educational workshops, etc. Coordinating logistics includes assisting with scheduling, room reservations, event set up, event communications, event materials, promotional signage, etc. Could also include attending evening and occasional weekend events as needed.</li><li>Administratively maintain outreach calendars, outreach metrics, event attendance, and recruitment outcomes having data ready to provide when requested.</li><li>Keep up with all inventory of marketing and recruitment materials, requesting an order of new supplies, as needed, including program T-Shirts.</li><li>Manage Education Mobility social media accounts and assist in developing engaging promotional content. Includes responding to social media messages, inquiries, and outreach communications in a professional and timely manner.</li><li>Create graphics, flyers, digital signage, promotional materials, and marketing campaigns for events and programs. Includes coordinating the distribution of marketing materials across campus and within the surrounding community.</li><li>Create, maintain, and update Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) for outreach activities, recruitment processes, and systems utilized by Education Abroad and Study in America.</li><li>Support passport office walk-in days directing the customer flow.</li></ul><div><br></div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58331 2026-08-28T11:01:58-05:00 2026-08-28T11:01:59-05:00 Accountant IV <div>Performs advanced, professional accounting functions that support the integrity of the university's financial reporting and accounting operations. Responsible for state appropriations, cash and investment accounting activities, including oversight of daily payment processing, reconciliation of financial data between the university's general ledger and the Uniform Statewide Accounting System (USAS), and participation in year-end financial reporting for the Annual Financial Report (AFR). Ensures compliance with governmental GAAP, State of Texas requirements, and other applicable accounting standards and regulations.</div> Financial Reporting <ul><li>Bachelor’s degree in accounting from an accredited United States (U.S.) university or may substitute for a completed degree with 18 accounting credit hours plus relevant experience;</li><li>Financial reporting and accounting experience;</li><li>Experience with complex reconciliations of separate financial systems;</li><li>Ability to analyze and apply accounting theory to complex transactions;</li><li>Proficient in Excel including an attention to detail;</li><li>Experience with problem solving and analytical writing</li><li>Ability to interpret existing and new federal, state, and local regulations and policies to ensure continued accounting and reporting compliance</li></ul> <ul><li>Experience with the Uniform Statewide Accounting System (USAS)</li><li>Certified Public Accountant</li><li>4 years of professional and progressive experience managing in a complex organization</li><li>Knowledge of State Comptroller reporting requirements and guidelines</li><li>Experience with investment accounting</li><li>Experience with an ERP system (Workday, SAP, or Banner)</li><li>Ability to develop and maintain working relationships with internal and external customers</li></ul> <div>Performs advanced, professional accounting functions that support the integrity of the university's financial reporting and accounting operations. Responsible for state appropriations, cash and investment accounting activities, including oversight of daily payment processing, reconciliation of financial data between the university's general ledger and the Uniform Statewide Accounting System (USAS), and participation in year-end financial reporting for the Annual Financial Report (AFR). Ensures compliance with governmental GAAP, State of Texas requirements, and other applicable accounting standards and regulations.</div> <ul><li>Manage and oversee the institution’s revenue appropriations and serve as the institutional liaison with the State Comptroller’s Office on accounting matters</li><li>Review monthly reconciliations between the university’s general ledger system and the Uniform Statewide Accounting System (USAS)</li><li>Oversee bank reconciliations and investment accounting</li><li>Participate in the monthly and year-end closing processes by preparing financial statements and reviewing the work of others</li><li>Develop, monitor, and report key financial ratios and metrics</li><li>Interpret and implement federal, state, system, and university policies and regulations</li><li>Design and document internal control procedures</li><li>Research and resolve financial reporting issues</li><li>Provide necessary training and technical assistance to staff</li><li>Assist with hiring decisions and conduct annual staff performance evaluations</li><li>Other duties as assigned</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58325 2026-08-27T16:14:31-05:00 2026-08-27T16:14:33-05:00 Air Conditioning Mech I <div>The University Facilities Management Department is seeking a motivated and dependable entry-level HVAC technician to join our maintenance team. This position assists with the installation, maintenance, troubleshooting, and repair of heating, ventilation, air conditioning, and refrigeration systems across campus buildings.</div> Facilities Operations <ul><li>High school diploma or GED.</li><li>EPA Section 608 Universal Certification.</li><li>One (1) year of HVAC employment/field experience.</li><li>Basic knowledge of HVAC principles, tools, and safety practices.</li><li>Ability to read and follow technical instructions and maintenance procedures.</li><li>Available and willing to work after-hours on-call duty, on a rotating basis with other shop personnel</li><li>Currently hold or have the ability to obtain a drivers license within 90 days of employment</li></ul> <ul><li>Familiarity with commercial HVAC systems and building automation systems (BAS).</li><li>Experience working in an educational or institutional environment.</li></ul> <div>The University Facilities Management Department is seeking a motivated and dependable entry-level HVAC technician to join our maintenance team. This position assists with the installation, maintenance, troubleshooting, and repair of heating, ventilation, air conditioning, and refrigeration systems across campus buildings.</div> <ul><li>Assist senior technicians with preventive maintenance and repairs of HVAC and refrigeration equipment.</li><li>Perform routine inspections of air handling units, exhaust fans, boilers, chillers, split systems, and related equipment.</li><li>Change filters, belts, bearings, and other maintenance components as required.</li><li>Monitor and document equipment performance and operating conditions.</li><li>Respond to service requests and support campus work orders.</li><li>Assist in diagnosing mechanical and electrical HVAC system issues.</li><li>Follow all university safety procedures and applicable regulations.</li><li>Support emergency response activities related to HVAC system failures or building comfort issues.</li><li>Participate in training programs and continuing education opportunities.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58324 2026-08-27T16:12:30-05:00 2026-08-27T16:12:31-05:00 Custodian <div>Responsible for enhancing the physical appearance of the buildings on campus by providing a sanitary environment and preventing the transmission of disease carrying microorganisms.</div> Student Center <ul><li>Knowledge of: Contaminated waste disposal universal practices and precautions; cleaning equipment operation, disinfecting agents, and chemicals; basic mechanical concepts; safety standards and procedures; characteristics of and techniques for using custodial equipment and supplies.</li><li>Skill in: Interacting courteously with others; working as a team member; inspecting work areas and reporting problems and hazards; prioritizing workload for self and others. e professional and courteous.</li><li>Ability to: Understand instructions to operate equipment, mix cleaners and labels on mixed bottles; perform basic math.</li></ul> <div>Responsible for enhancing the physical appearance of the buildings on campus by providing a sanitary environment and preventing the transmission of disease carrying microorganisms.</div> <ul><li>Empty trash cans and dispose of garbage.</li><li>Empty recycling cans/cardboard and place in designated pick up area.</li><li>Clean and disinfect sinks and bathrooms and restock paper products. Vacuum carpets.</li><li>Vacuum carpets: Hallways, Ballrooms, Meeting Rooms, and Common Areas.</li><li>Clean and care for hard floors. Buff and polish vinyl floors as needed.</li><li>Dust surfaces in common areas, ballrooms, meeting rooms, stairwells, and hallways.</li><li>Clean lobbies, common areas, study rooms, laundries, offices, furniture, chalk and writing boards, and light fixtures.</li><li>Secure buildings, entrances, exits, interior doors, custodial closets, storage rooms, etc.</li><li>Clean interior and exterior windows.</li><li>Clean Ballroom kitchens and stock with soap and paper products.</li><li>Maintain supplies, keys, equipment, and custodial closet.</li><li>Operate all custodial equipment: floor scrubbers, carpets extractors, vacuums.</li><li>Extract carpeting: Ballrooms, Meeting Rooms, Study Lounges, Hallways, Offices, and common areas.</li><li>Clean and maintain all custodial equipment after each use and report needed repairs to supervisor.</li><li>Report any building deficiency's to supervisor: Lights out, broken fixtures/furniture, stains, small repairs and paint needs.</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58319 2026-08-27T14:52:53-05:00 2026-08-27T14:52:54-05:00 Air Conditioning Mechanic II <div>The University is seeking a skilled and motivated HVAC Technician II to join our Facilities Services team. This mid-level position is responsible for installing, maintaining, troubleshooting, and repairing heating, ventilation, air conditioning, and refrigeration (HVAC/R) systems across academic buildings, laboratories, residence halls, athletic facilities, and administrative spaces.</div> Facilities Operations <ul><li>High school diploma or GED.</li><li>Technical school training or three (3) years of HVAC employment/field experience.</li><li>EPA Section 608 Universal Certification.</li><li>Working knowledge of HVAC controls, electrical systems, and refrigeration principles.</li><li>Ability to diagnose and repair mechanical, electrical, and control-related equipment issues.</li><li>Ability to read and follow technical instructions and maintenance procedures.</li><li>Available and willing to work after-hours on-call duty, on a rotating basis with other shop personnel</li><li>Currently hold or have the ability to obtain a drivers license within 90 days of employment?<br><br></li></ul> <ul><li>Experience working in a university, government, or large institutional environment.</li><li>Experience with Building Automation Systems (BAS), such as Siemens, Johnson Controls, Honeywell, or Schneider Electric.</li><li>Additional certifications such as HVAC Excellence, NATE, or trade licenses.</li><li>Knowledge of energy management and sustainability practices.</li></ul><div><br></div> <div>The University is seeking a skilled and motivated HVAC Technician II to join our Facilities Services team. This mid-level position is responsible for installing, maintaining, troubleshooting, and repairing heating, ventilation, air conditioning, and refrigeration (HVAC/R) systems across academic buildings, laboratories, residence halls, athletic facilities, and administrative spaces.</div> <ul><li>Perform preventive maintenance, inspections, and repairs on HVAC and refrigeration systems.</li><li>Troubleshoot and diagnose issues involving chillers, boilers, pumps, air handlers, VAV systems, cooling towers, and building automation systems (BAS).</li><li>Install, replace, and repair HVAC equipment, motors, controls, thermostats, and related components.</li><li>Monitor and adjust building environmental systems to maintain occupant comfort and operational efficiency.</li><li>Respond to service requests and emergency maintenance calls in a timely manner.</li><li>Read and interpret blueprints, schematics, wiring diagrams, and technical manuals.</li><li>Maintain accurate records of work performed, materials used, and equipment condition.</li><li>Assist with campus energy conservation initiatives and sustainability programs.</li><li>Ensure all work is completed in accordance with applicable safety regulations, codes, and University policies.</li><li>Collaborate with other Facilities Services personnel, contractors, and campus stakeholders.</li></ul><div><br></div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58318 2026-08-27T14:23:49-05:00 2026-08-27T14:23:51-05:00 Campus Expression & Community Standards Coordinator <div>Reporting to the Associate Vice President for Student Success and Dean of Students, the Campus Expression &amp; Community Standards Coordinator provides primary operational coordination for the university’s expressive activity monitoring and response program, including both administrative operations and real-time campus response. The position coordinates expressive activity readiness and response protocols; event monitoring and documentation; deployment and coordination of campus responders; communication with campus partners; tracking and maintaining records; and post-event follow-up. The position works closely with the Dean of Students Office, University Police Department (UPD), Environmental, Health, Safety, Risk and Emergency Management (EHSREM), and other university partners to support consistent, coordinated, and compliant responses that protect free expression while promoting campus safety and adherence to university policy.<br><br></div><div>The Campus Expression &amp; Community Standards Coordinator also supports large-event student behavior monitoring and response, divisional compliance tracking and reporting, and Student Conduct and Community Standards. This position serves as an investigator for complex student conduct cases and provides additional investigative support as needed. Across these responsibilities, the position supports effective coordination, accurate documentation and reporting, student accountability, and institutional compliance.</div> Health & Wellbeing <ul><li>Bachelor’s degree in higher education, student affairs, public administration, criminal justice, or a related field</li><li>Experience coordinating programs, operations, or cross-functional initiatives</li><li>Demonstrated ability to manage sensitive situations with sound judgment and discretion</li><li>Strong collaboration and communication skills, with the ability to operate effectively in dynamic environments</li><li>Ability to work evenings and weekends as required, including on-call responsibilities during high-visibility events or urgent situations</li><li>Knowledge of freedom of expression/speech laws and policies, particularly as applicable to public college campuses</li><li>Strong facilitation, documentation, and report-writing skills</li><li>Sound judgment under pressure with a focus on de-escalation and operational consistency</li><li>Experience supporting expressive activity, demonstrations, or large-scale event response</li></ul><div><br></div> <ul><li>Master’s degree in higher education, student affairs, criminal justice, or related field</li><li>Experience conducting student conduct investigations and/or adjudication</li><li>Ability to coordinate across multiple stakeholders, including law enforcement and compliance units</li></ul> <div>Reporting to the Associate Vice President for Student Success and Dean of Students, the Campus Expression &amp; Community Standards Coordinator provides primary operational coordination for the university’s expressive activity monitoring and response program, including both administrative operations and real-time campus response. The position coordinates expressive activity readiness and response protocols; event monitoring and documentation; deployment and coordination of campus responders; communication with campus partners; tracking and maintaining records; and post-event follow-up. The position works closely with the Dean of Students Office, University Police Department (UPD), Environmental, Health, Safety, Risk and Emergency Management (EHSREM), and other university partners to support consistent, coordinated, and compliant responses that protect free expression while promoting campus safety and adherence to university policy.<br><br></div><div>The Campus Expression &amp; Community Standards Coordinator also supports large-event student behavior monitoring and response, divisional compliance tracking and reporting, and Student Conduct and Community Standards. This position serves as an investigator for complex student conduct cases and provides additional investigative support as needed. Across these responsibilities, the position supports effective coordination, accurate documentation and reporting, student accountability, and institutional compliance.</div> <div><strong>Expressive Activity Program Coordination, Monitoring, and Response</strong></div><ul><li>Coordinate the administrative and real-time operations of the university’s Expressive Activity Monitoring and Response Program, ensuring consistent implementation of university policies, procedures, and response protocols.</li><li>Coordinate the Expressive Activity Response Team (EART), including responder recruitment and training, on-call schedules, activation and notification protocols, deployment, documentation, and after-action processes.</li><li>Monitor and track expressive activities across university locations and maintain accurate records of planned and unplanned activities, university response, emerging concerns, and outcomes.</li><li>Coordinate readiness planning for demonstrations, speakers, counter-demonstrations, protests, and other high-visibility expressive activities, including staffing, communication, documentation, de-escalation, and escalation protocols.</li><li>Serve as a primary on-site coordinator for expressive activities, facilitating communication and coordinated response among university responders and campus partners.</li><li>Provide real-time guidance regarding university expressive activity policies, freedom of expression, time, place, and manner requirements, and established campus procedures.</li><li>Coordinate with UPD, EHSREM, Student Involvement and Engagement, and other campus partners to assess operational and safety considerations and determine appropriate university response.</li><li>Proactively engage student organizations, advisors, event organizers, and campus partners to support awareness of and compliance with expressive activity requirements.</li><li>Develop and deliver training, guidance, and resources for university personnel responsible for monitoring or responding to expressive activities.</li><li>Conduct post-event reviews and prepare event summaries, after-action reports, trend analyses, and recommendations to strengthen institutional preparedness and response.</li><li>Analyze expressive activity data and emerging trends to identify operational needs, potential risks, and opportunities for continuous improvement.</li></ul><div><strong>Large-Event Student Behavior Monitoring and Response</strong></div><ul><li>Coordinate student behavior monitoring and response for athletic events, commencements, major campus programs, and other high-attendance or high-visibility university events.</li><li>Assist with developing event-specific staffing, communication, documentation, escalation, and response protocols in collaboration with appropriate campus partners.</li><li>Serve in an on-site coordination role during designated events, supporting de-escalation, community standards, policy compliance, and appropriate referral of incidents.</li><li>Document significant student behavior incidents and coordinate referrals to Student Conduct and Community Standards or other appropriate university offices for follow-up.</li><li>Identify recurring student behavior trends and recommend education, prevention, or operational strategies to reduce future concerns.</li></ul><div><strong>Student Conduct Investigations and Case Support</strong></div><ul><li>Serve as an investigator for complex Student Conduct and Community Standards cases and provide additional investigative capacity when needed.</li><li>Conduct neutral, thorough, and timely investigations into alleged violations of the Code of Student Conduct and other applicable university policies.</li><li>Gather and analyze information, conduct interviews, review relevant records and evidence, and prepare investigative reports, findings, and case materials consistent with established procedures.</li><li>Maintain appropriate investigative records and coordinate with Student Conduct and Community Standards leadership throughout the investigative process.</li></ul><div><strong>Divisional Compliance and Risk Management Support</strong></div><ul><li>Support the Division of Student Success compliance reporting program, including tracking reporting requirements and deadlines and coordinating the collection, verification, organization, and submission of required information.</li><li>Assist divisional units in maintaining documentation and records necessary to demonstrate compliance with applicable university, system, state, and federal requirements.</li><li>Serve on the Division of Student Success Risk Management Committee.</li><li>Assist with identifying and assessing operational, safety, compliance, and reputational risks affecting divisional programs and activities.</li><li>Translate applicable policies and requirements into operational guidance, workflows, tools, and training to support consistent implementation.</li><li>Assist with compliance, risk, and trend reports for divisional leadership and monitor completion of identified corrective or mitigation actions.</li></ul><div><strong>Emergency Preparedness and Response</strong></div><ul><li>Support Division of Student Success responsibilities related to campus emergency preparedness and response, particularly when incidents involve students, expressive activity, or large campus events.</li><li>Participate in coordinated university response efforts and assist with implementing established communication, documentation, escalation, and after-hours response protocols.</li><li>Collaborate with UPD, EHSREM, the Dean of Students Office, and other campus partners during emergencies and significant incidents affecting students or the campus community.</li><li>Participate in emergency preparedness exercises, after-action reviews, and improvement planning relevant to the position’s responsibilities.</li><li>This position is designated as essential personnel and may require availability to work evenings, weekends, and during emergency or critical operations as needed.</li></ul><div><strong>General Administrative and Professional Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>Maintain high standards of confidentiality, professionalism, neutrality, accuracy, and documentation across all assigned responsibilities.</li><li>Maintain current knowledge of university policies and applicable requirements related to expressive activity, student conduct, institutional compliance, and emergency response.</li><li>Serve on committees, task forces, and divisional initiatives related to assigned responsibilities.</li><li>Support assessment and continuous improvement of processes related to expressive activity, large-event response, student conduct, compliance, and risk management.</li><li>Perform other related duties as assigned in support of the Division of Student Success and Dean of Students Office.</li></ul><div><strong>Other Duties</strong></div><ul><li>Perform additional duties as assigned by the Associate Vice President for Student Success and Dean of Students to support the broader goals of the Division of Student Success and contribute to the continued success of the university.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58313 2026-08-27T08:16:04-05:00 2026-08-27T08:16:05-05:00 Social Science Researcher <div>The Texas School Safety Center (TxSSC) is an official university-level research center at Texas State University. The TxSSC is tasked in Chapter 37 of the Texas Education Code and the Governor’s Homeland Security Strategic Plan with key school safety initiatives and mandates. The TxSSC serves as the clearinghouse for the dissemination of safety and security information through research, training, and technical assistance for K-12 schools and junior colleges throughout the state of Texas. As a result, Texas has become a national leader in school safety practices and is relied upon for assistance and guidance from jurisdictions throughout the nation.</div><div>The TxSSC welcomes highly qualified candidates to apply for a <em>Social Science Researcher </em>position in the Research and Evaluation (R&amp;E) Division. The primary responsibility of this position is to conduct scholarly research focused on school safety and security. The R&amp;E Division is currently involved in projects connected to leadership and incident command during emergency situations, security personnel on school campuses, emergency planning for students, gun storage practices, teacher victimization, and school behavioral threat assessment.</div><div>The successful candidate will expand the capabilities of the TxSSC and have the unique opportunity to be part of a collaborative team who support each other in project conceptualization, study design, field implementation (quantitative, qualitative, and mixed methods), analysis, and dissemination of research and evaluation findings to various stakeholder groups. <strong>All research and evaluation efforts aim to ensure that schools and communities across Texas are safe, secure, and healthy learning environments.</strong></div> Texas School Safety Center <ul><li>Master’s Degree in criminology, education, psychology, sociology, public policy, or related field.</li><li>A minimum of three (3) years of professional experience conducting applied social science research or educational research.</li><li>Demonstrated experience designing and applying social science research methodologies.</li><li>Demonstrated experience developing data collection instruments for social sciences (e.g., surveys, interview protocols, or rubrics, etc.), including managing surveys with standard survey software (e.g., Qualtrics).</li><li>Demonstrated experience applying quantitative social science techniques (e.g., regression, ANOVA, etc.) using software packages (e.g., SPSS).</li><li>Demonstrated experience with qualitative analysis techniques and software packages (e.g., NVivo).</li><li>Highly attentive to detail and organization.</li></ul> <ul><li>Demonstrated experience conducting research directly related to educational environments.</li><li>Five (5) or more years of professional experience conducting applied social science research or educational research.</li><li>Documented educational training or research experience related to one or more of the following fields: mental health in school-aged children, youth involvement in school safety, school-based law enforcement, or behavioral threat assessments.</li><li>Demonstrated experience in technical, public policy, and/or legislative writing (outside of work related to academic degree).</li><li>Demonstrated experience with one or more of the following techniques: meta-analysis, advanced statistical sampling, and survey validation.</li><li>Experience navigating Institutional Review Board (IRB) processes and human subjects protection protocols in educational or community settings.</li><li>Documented authorship in peer-reviewed journal(s).</li><li>Documented experience writing grant proposals.</li><li>Demonstrated knowledge of Chapter 37 of the Texas Education Code.</li><li>Demonstrated experience working with external collaborators and/or research participants on projects not associated with course work.</li></ul> <div>The Texas School Safety Center (TxSSC) is an official university-level research center at Texas State University. The TxSSC is tasked in Chapter 37 of the Texas Education Code and the Governor’s Homeland Security Strategic Plan with key school safety initiatives and mandates. The TxSSC serves as the clearinghouse for the dissemination of safety and security information through research, training, and technical assistance for K-12 schools and junior colleges throughout the state of Texas. As a result, Texas has become a national leader in school safety practices and is relied upon for assistance and guidance from jurisdictions throughout the nation.</div><div>The TxSSC welcomes highly qualified candidates to apply for a <em>Social Science Researcher </em>position in the Research and Evaluation (R&amp;E) Division. The primary responsibility of this position is to conduct scholarly research focused on school safety and security. The R&amp;E Division is currently involved in projects connected to leadership and incident command during emergency situations, security personnel on school campuses, emergency planning for students, gun storage practices, teacher victimization, and school behavioral threat assessment.</div><div>The successful candidate will expand the capabilities of the TxSSC and have the unique opportunity to be part of a collaborative team who support each other in project conceptualization, study design, field implementation (quantitative, qualitative, and mixed methods), analysis, and dissemination of research and evaluation findings to various stakeholder groups. <strong>All research and evaluation efforts aim to ensure that schools and communities across Texas are safe, secure, and healthy learning environments.</strong></div> <ul><li>Design appropriate methodologies to address topics related to school safety and security.</li><li>Conduct literature reviews on topics related to school safety and security.</li><li>Design and administer data collection procedures including surveys, focus groups, and interview protocols, as well as other appropriate data collection procedures.</li><li>Conduct rigorous mixed-methods analysis, synthesizing quantitative survey results with qualitative narrative data.</li><li>Stay current on innovative social science research methodologies and field-based data collection strategies.</li><li>Disseminate information clearly and concisely in verbal and written formats to a variety of stakeholders including researchers and practitioners.</li><li>Develop and contribute to written reports for internal and external stakeholders, scholarly articles for peer-reviewed journals, grant proposals for private and government entities, scholarly presentations for national and state conferences, and other research-related products.</li><li>Organize project materials by keeping detailed records to ensure research activities are well-documented.</li><li>Provide training and support for other team members on qualitative and quantitative analysis techniques.</li><li>Assist in survey administration, sample design, and dataset curation for annual statewide surveys and TxSSC trainings and events as needed; assist with training evaluations and yearly assessments of programs and activities as needed.</li><li>Provide technical support to school stakeholders and internal staff in a professional manner.</li><li>Work collaboratively and professionally with all divisions of the TxSSC.</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58311 2026-08-26T16:44:41-05:00 2026-08-26T16:44:42-05:00 Director, TXST One Stop <div>The TXST One Stop works with the offices of Admissions, Financial Aid and Scholarships, Student Business Services, and University Registrar to assist students and their families with navigating the admissions, financial aid, and payment processes.</div> TXST One Stop <ul><li>Bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of training and experience</li><li>Managerial experience</li><li>Supervisory experience</li><li>Higher education experience</li></ul> <ul><li>Two years of managerial experience and strong managerial skills</li><li>Two years of supervisory experience and excellent supervisory skills</li><li>Excellent customer service skills</li><li>Ability to easily adapt and learn quickly</li><li>Demonstrated initiative</li><li>Proven problem-solving and critical thinking skills</li><li>Highly proficient written and verbal communicator</li><li>Exceptional interpersonal and public speaking skills</li><li>Proven ability to work independently and as a team</li><li>Strong organizational skills</li><li>Proficient with PC, student information systems, and customer relationship management systems</li></ul> <div>The TXST One Stop works with the offices of Admissions, Financial Aid and Scholarships, Student Business Services, and University Registrar to assist students and their families with navigating the admissions, financial aid, and payment processes.</div> <div>The Director, reporting to the Associate Vice President for TXST Global Operations, will manage the day-to-day One Stop operations. The position assesses the performance of direct reports via quality assurance measures, assesses overall customer service metrics, and directs operational changes to ensure the delivery of excellent service. The Director also works with home office department heads to facilitate seamless collaborations. The position will make sure their team is closely working with students to help them understand everything from the application process to paying their semester bill. The position is important to the overall Enrollment Plan in effectively facilitating students’ decisions to attend Texas State and then persist with their enrollment to graduation. Excellent communication skills and customer service are essential to this position. Also essential to this role is the ability to critically analyze processes and provide recommendations to improve them (thus, improving the student journey), as well as the ability to navigate resources, policies, and procedures across multiple on-campus departments.<br><br><strong>Job Duties</strong></div><ul><li>Manage day-to-day One Stop operations</li><li>Develop, refine, and drive the meeting of key performance indictors</li><li>Regularly assess customer service and performance data to anticipate and proactively address student needs</li><li>Work collaboratively with home office department heads to ensure One Stop operations are effectively addressing related student and parent needs</li><li>Develop and help train direct reports to ensure their success</li><li>Assess direct reports and provide feedback to facilitate their success and that of students</li><li>Establish, monitor, and drive needed changes to assessment metrics (i.e., staff performance, customer satisfaction, etc.)</li><li>Manage effectively and efficiently escalations from staff</li><li>Establish, assess, and manage needed improvements to technology to meet the One Stop mission</li><li>Oversee the development and maintenance of office policies and procedures</li><li>Assess potential enrollment barriers related to business processes and provide home office department heads with input on how these barriers might be addressed</li><li>Navigate confidential student information across multiple systems</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58307 2026-08-26T15:40:31-05:00 2026-08-26T15:40:34-05:00 Senior Network Administrator <div>Texas State University is hiring a Sr. Network Administrator to help design, operate, secure, and modernize the university’s multi-campus network infrastructure. This is a senior technical role responsible for supporting enterprise wired, wireless, data center, security, and wide-area network services used across the university.</div><div>The position works with a broad range of network technologies, including routing and switching, network fabrics, data center networks, wireless infrastructure, SD-WAN, network security platforms, Cisco ISE, monitoring systems, and automation tools. The successful candidate will be expected to provide technical leadership, solve complex problems, contribute to network architecture decisions, and help deliver infrastructure projects from planning through implementation.<br><br><strong>About the Job<br></strong><br></div><div>Texas State University operates a large, heterogeneous network environment supporting academic, administrative, residential, research, and campus life services. The network includes equipment and platforms from multiple manufacturers, including Cisco, Juniper, HP/Aruba, and Ruckus Wireless. The team emphasizes reliable service delivery, standards-based design, operational consistency, security, documentation, and continuous improvement.</div><div>This role will have meaningful technical ownership in the operation and evolution of the campus network. Responsibilities include both hands-on administration and higher-level engineering work, such as developing standards, improving network reliability, leading technical projects, mentoring other staff, and coordinating with vendors and campus stakeholders.</div> Network Operations <ul><li>Five years of professional experience in network administration, network engineering, or closely related enterprise network infrastructure work.</li><li>Professional experience administering enterprise routing and switching infrastructure in a production environment.</li><li>Professional experience with dynamic routing protocols, such as BGP, OSPF, IS-IS, or EIGRP.</li><li>Professional experience supporting enterprise wireless networking technologies.</li><li>Professional experience supporting network security technologies, such as firewalls, IPS/IDS, network access control, Cisco ISE, segmentation, or related security platforms.</li></ul> <ul><li>Experience supporting data center network infrastructure.</li><li>Experience with network fabric technologies, such as EVPN/VXLAN, Cisco SDA, ACI, virtualized routing, or comparable fabric-based architectures.</li><li>Experience supporting MPLS, VRF, SD-WAN, or complex WAN routing environments.</li><li>Experience with Cisco ISE, NAC, 802.1X, device profiling, guest access, posture, or network segmentation.</li><li>Experience with network automation using Python, Ansible, APIs, Git, configuration management systems, or similar tools.</li><li>Experience working in higher education, government, large enterprise, healthcare, or another complex multi-site environment.</li><li>Current or prior network-related certifications, such as CCNP, CCIE, JNCIP, CWNP, Aruba, Ruckus, Fortinet, Palo Alto, or comparable credentials.</li></ul> <div>Texas State University is hiring a Sr. Network Administrator to help design, operate, secure, and modernize the university’s multi-campus network infrastructure. This is a senior technical role responsible for supporting enterprise wired, wireless, data center, security, and wide-area network services used across the university.</div><div>The position works with a broad range of network technologies, including routing and switching, network fabrics, data center networks, wireless infrastructure, SD-WAN, network security platforms, Cisco ISE, monitoring systems, and automation tools. The successful candidate will be expected to provide technical leadership, solve complex problems, contribute to network architecture decisions, and help deliver infrastructure projects from planning through implementation.<br><br><strong>About the Job<br></strong><br></div><div>Texas State University operates a large, heterogeneous network environment supporting academic, administrative, residential, research, and campus life services. The network includes equipment and platforms from multiple manufacturers, including Cisco, Juniper, HP/Aruba, and Ruckus Wireless. The team emphasizes reliable service delivery, standards-based design, operational consistency, security, documentation, and continuous improvement.</div><div>This role will have meaningful technical ownership in the operation and evolution of the campus network. Responsibilities include both hands-on administration and higher-level engineering work, such as developing standards, improving network reliability, leading technical projects, mentoring other staff, and coordinating with vendors and campus stakeholders.</div> <ul><li>Design, administer, maintain, and troubleshoot enterprise network infrastructure, including campus routing and switching, wireless, data center networks, network fabrics, WAN/SD-WAN, and related services.</li><li>Support network security and access control platforms, including Cisco ISE, network segmentation, authentication/authorization policies, and related security integrations.</li><li>Diagnose and resolve complex network incidents affecting wired, wireless, data center, WAN, and security services.</li><li>Lead and support network infrastructure projects from planning through implementation, including design, change coordination, testing, documentation, and operational handoff.</li><li>Develop and maintain network standards, diagrams, procedures, configuration templates, and operational documentation.</li><li>Monitor network performance, availability, capacity, and reliability; identify trends and recommend improvements.</li><li>Automate network operations using scripting, APIs, configuration management tools, monitoring platforms, and AI-assisted workflows where appropriate.</li><li>Provide technical leadership, mentorship, and vendor coordination; participate in a shared after-hours on-call rotation, currently one week every six weeks.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58306 2026-08-26T15:12:41-05:00 2026-08-26T15:12:44-05:00 Academic Advisor I <div>Responsible for providing quality undergraduate advice to current and prospective students, and serves as a resource for them and their parents.</div> AA-Health Professions <ul><li>Bachelor's Degree</li><li>Documented work experience with college students or children/adolescents in a professional or volunteer capacity.</li><li>Demonstrated skill using Microsoft Office suite, specifically Microsoft Word, Excel, and Powerpoint. (Must indicate specific software applications with which you have experience on the application, resume or cover letter)</li><li>Evidence of attention to detail, as demonstrated in a grammatically correct cover letter and complete application.</li></ul> <ul><li>Professional academic advising experience in higher education.</li><li>Demonstrated professional knowledge of Texas State academic policies and procedures.</li><li>Demonstrated experience using Degree Works degree audit software in a professional capacity.</li><li>Knowledge of NACADA core competencies, core values and theories of acaemdic advising.</li></ul> <div>Responsible for providing quality undergraduate advice to current and prospective students, and serves as a resource for them and their parents.</div> <div>o The Academic Advisor I, under supervision, provides quality academic advising to new, continuing, and returning undergraduate students at Texas State University. The Academic Advisor I also provides appropriate advising guidance and referrals for prospective and visiting students.</div><div>· Job Duties</div><div>o Provide accurate and consistent information about major, degree requirements, and progress toward graduation</div><div>o Clearly explain complex information related to institutional policies and procedures</div><div>o Coordinate, plan, and prepare for advising sessions</div><div>o Engage with undergraduate students in-person, virtually, and over the phone</div><div>o Help undergraduate students define and develop realistic educational and career goals</div><div>o Maintain confidential student records through accurate and thorough documentation</div><ul><li>Review graduation applications and certify students’ eligibility for graduation</li></ul><div>o Maintain collaborative relationships with academic units and university partners</div><div>o Acknowledge and research student concerns, collaborate with appropriate stakeholders, and advocate for solutions with a commitment to fairness and integrity</div><div>o Refer undergraduate students to appropriate resources for assistance</div><div>o Participate in university efforts toward recruitment and retention such as Bobcat Day and New Student Orientation</div><div>o Provide recommendations for continuous improvement of advising services and integrate practices aimed at improving the student experience</div><div>o Commit to ongoing professional development and attainment of knowledge regarding industry advancements and best practices in academic advising</div><div>o Provide clerical assistance as needed</div><div>o Complete work at the request of other campus offices to support processes related to accreditation and/or student degree progress (Satisfactory Academic Progress plans, Courses Counting Toward Degree, Athletic Academic Progress forms, Transfer Course Agreements, etc.)</div><div>o Other duties as assigned</div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58302 2026-08-26T13:44:03-05:00 2026-08-26T13:44:06-05:00 Dispatcher <div>The Dispatcher is responsible for receiving and prioritizing incoming calls for assistance from the university and managing and directing responding units.</div> UPD Communications/Records <ul><li>High school diploma or GED equivalent.</li><li>Demonstrated ability to effectively multitask in a fast-paced environment while maintaining accuracy and attention to detail.</li><li>Strong customer service and interpersonal communication skills with the ability to interact professionally and courteously with students, faculty, staff, visitors, emergency responders, and the public.</li><li>Basic computer proficiency and the ability to learn and utilize multiple software applications, databases, and communication systems simultaneously.</li><li>Ability to make sound decisions, prioritize competing demands, and remain calm and composed during stressful and emergency situations.</li><li>Ability to communicate clearly and effectively, both verbally and in writing.</li><li>Current Texas Commission on Law Enforcement (TCOLE) Telecommunicator License or the ability to obtain certification within one (1) year of employment in accordance with state requirements.</li></ul><div><br></div> <ul><li>Associate degree or higher from an accredited college or university.</li><li>Previous experience in public safety communications, emergency dispatch, law enforcement, fire, EMS, military, call center operations, or a high-volume customer service environment.</li><li>Working knowledge of public safety communications principles, emergency response procedures, and computer-aided dispatch (CAD) systems.</li><li>Knowledge of Texas Crime Information Center (TCIC), National Crime Information Center (NCIC), Texas Law Enforcement Telecommunications System (TLETS), and National Law Enforcement Telecommunications System (NLETS) policies and procedures.</li><li>Knowledge of emergency medical dispatch (EMD) principles and protocols.</li><li>Familiarity with security alarm monitoring, video surveillance systems, or other public safety technology.</li><li>Knowledge of Texas State University policies and procedures, University Police Department General Orders, and Communications Standard Operating Procedures.</li><li>Current Texas Commission on Law Enforcement (TCOLE) Telecommunicator License.</li><li>Bilingual communication skills are desirable.</li></ul><div><br></div> <div>The Dispatcher is responsible for receiving and prioritizing incoming calls for assistance from the university and managing and directing responding units.</div> <ul><li>Accurately track the status and location of emergency personnel using sophisticated computer software.</li><li>Monitor and respond to alarms, including security access, fire alarm systems, security cameras, closed-circuit television, teletype, and TDD systems.</li><li>Manage, monitor, and enter data specific to Open Fox.</li><li>Handle calls for police or other university services, including those from emergency phones and 911 systems.</li><li>Gather information swiftly and precisely.</li><li>Manage radio communications and other information directed to police or university staff.</li><li>Perform other related duties as required.</li></ul><div><br></div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58301 2026-08-26T13:41:12-05:00 2026-08-26T13:41:14-05:00 Coordinator, Team Operations <div>The Coordinator of Team Operations assists the head coach in the organization, management and administration of strategies as they relate to the goals and objectives of the football program.</div> Football <ul><li>Knowledge of intercollegiate rules and regulations.</li><li>Prior work experience in intercollegiate or professional football operations.</li><li>Knowledge of general university policies and procedures.</li><li>Skill in oral communication and public relations.</li><li>Knowledge of Microsoft Office programs, including Word and Excel.</li></ul> <ul><li>Bachelors’ degree with additional consideration for Masters.</li></ul> <div>The Coordinator of Team Operations assists the head coach in the organization, management and administration of strategies as they relate to the goals and objectives of the football program.</div> <div>Position duties include:</div><ul><li>Prepare and manage financial aspects of the football program, including, but not limited to budget, travel, operations, and fundraising in consultation with Head Coach.</li><li>Serve as the main liaison with the department of athletics external operations, internal operations, NCAA compliance and business offices.</li><li>Monitor academic progress of football student-athletes, assist in the development and implementation of public relations, marketing and fundraising initiatives for the program and the athletic department.</li><li>Comply with applicable NCAA, Conference and Texas State University rules and regulations.</li><li>Other duties as assigned by the Head Football Coach.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58297 2026-08-26T12:46:50-05:00 2026-08-26T12:46:51-05:00 Financial Operations Specialist <div>The FinOps Specialist performs financial operations and cloud cost management activities in support of the IT Division. This position works collaboratively with IT Finance, IT Procurement, and Central Systems Operations and is responsible for monitoring and analyzing cloud expenditures, usage, budgets, forecasts, billing, and financial performance to promote cost transparency, accountability, and efficient use of cloud resources.</div> VP for Information Technology <ul><li>Knowledge of financial operations principles and frameworks, including cost allocation, budgeting, forecasting, optimization, and financial accountability.</li><li>Knowledge of cloud financial management and pricing models, including consumption-based billing, reserved capacity, savings plans, commitments, licensing, and other cloud cost-management concepts.</li><li>Understanding of cloud infrastructure, including compute, storage, networking, databases, software licensing, and other technology services, sufficient to interpret cost drivers and spending patterns.</li><li>Skill in analyzing and reconciling financial and cloud consumption data, identifying cost trends and anomalies, developing forecasts, preparing reports and dashboards, and recommending opportunities for cost optimization.</li><li>Ability to work collaboratively across organizational functions, manage multiple priorities, communicate effectively, organize complex financial and technical information, and provide recommendations to management and stakeholders.</li></ul> <ul><li>FinOps or cloud-related certifications.</li><li>Experience using cloud cost-management, optimization, reporting, or dashboarding tools.</li></ul><div><br></div> <div>The FinOps Specialist performs financial operations and cloud cost management activities in support of the IT Division. This position works collaboratively with IT Finance, IT Procurement, and Central Systems Operations and is responsible for monitoring and analyzing cloud expenditures, usage, budgets, forecasts, billing, and financial performance to promote cost transparency, accountability, and efficient use of cloud resources.</div> <ul><li>Monitor and analyze cloud usage, costs, budgets, forecasts, and financial performance to identify trends, anomalies, optimization opportunities, and potential budget impacts, while developing and maintaining cost models and financial reports to support organizational planning and decision-making.</li><li>Review and reconcile cloud invoices, billing data, purchase orders, contracts, and financial records; investigate discrepancies and coordinate their resolution with the appropriate departments and vendors.</li><li>Develop and maintain cost allocation, tagging, chargeback, and cost management methodologies to accurately assign cloud expenditures to departments, applications, projects, and other organizational units.</li><li>Identify and recommend cloud cost optimization opportunities, including resource rightsizing, elimination of unused resources, commitment-based discounts, licensing optimization, and improvements to cloud architecture and consumption practices.</li><li>Track cost savings, cost avoidance, utilization, and other FinOps performance measures; prepare reports and dashboards to communicate financial performance and optimization results.</li><li>Collaborate with Finance, Procurement, and Central Systems Operations to establish cloud budgets, manage expenditures, improve forecasting, and promote financial accountability.</li><li>Assist with the development, implementation, and maintenance of FinOps policies, procedures, standards, controls, and governance practices for cloud financial management.</li><li>Perform related duties and special projects as assigned.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58286 2026-08-25T08:38:59-05:00 2026-08-25T08:39:01-05:00 Web & Mobile Strategy Manager <div>Develop marketing and communications strategy that drives increased awareness and engagement with internal and external audiences.</div> University Marketing <ul><li>Bachelor’s degree in communications, marketing, information technology, or a related field.</li><li>Minimum five years of experience in web program management, digital strategy, CMS administration, enterprise web projects, or a closely related field.</li></ul> <ul><li>Advanced degree in communications, marketing, information technology, business administration, or a related discipline.</li><li>Experience in higher education.</li><li>Experience with multisite network ecosystem and site architecture, web governance, mobile application strategy, SEO/AEO initiatives, and user experience planning.</li></ul> <div>Develop marketing and communications strategy that drives increased awareness and engagement with internal and external audiences.</div> <ul><li>Lead the division's web strategy by developing and implementing SEO and Answer Engine Optimization (AEO) initiatives, content optimization strategies, user experience improvements, and digital best practices that strengthen the university's web presence and support institutional priorities. Evaluate emerging technologies and recommend enhancements that improve discoverability, accessibility, and engagement.</li><li>Provide strategic leadership for the university website and TXST Mobile app by establishing content priorities, improving user experience, supporting governance of mobile communications, and coordinating enhancements that improve audience engagement and digital effectiveness.</li><li>Represent the division on the Web Governance Committee; develop and maintain web standards, accessibility compliance, quality assurance processes, and governance procedures. Partner with campus stakeholders to support the health, consistency, and long-term sustainability of the university's web ecosystem.</li><li>Serve as the division's primary liaison to Mobile/Web Systems by coordinating web and mobile development priorities, platform enhancements, project requests, and strategic initiatives. Manage the division's web project portfolio, prioritize initiatives, coordinate campus partners, and ensure successful completion of web and mobile projects.</li><li>Monitor the health and performance of division-owned websites by conducting quality assurance reviews, identifying broken links and content issues, monitoring analytics, evaluating campaign and core-page performance, and recommending improvements based on user behavior and digital performance metrics.</li><li>Provide leadership, direction, coaching, and performance management for the UI/UX Designer and two Content Strategists; establish priorities and support professional development.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58279 2026-08-24T11:26:43-05:00 2026-08-24T11:26:45-05:00 Landscape Specialist <div>Assist the Director of Grounds in developing and maintaining a high-quality tier 1 landscape by performing quality assurance duties, identifying landscape improvement and renovation needs, assist in designing new beds, and identifying plant replacement needs. Ensure new landscape establishment.</div> Facilities Services <ul><li>Ability to communicate, receive and assign instructions, direct work, recognize and change priorities. Good oral and written communication skills.</li><li>Ability to determine acceptable work quality and quantity.</li><li>Ability to work independently and in a team environment to handle complex projects, prioritize and manage multiple tasks under deadlines.</li><li>Ability to lift and carry items weighing up to 50 lbs., and perform strenuous physical duties for an entire shift.</li><li>Ability to work outdoors in extreme and varying weather conditions.</li><li>Ability to operate industry equipment for extended periods.</li><li>Knowledge and application of safety practices related to job duties, and safe use of industry related equipment.</li><li>Ability to perform Job Hazard Analysis.</li><li>A commitment to quality, customer service, personal development and safety.</li><li>Must be able to attain TDA pesticide applicator’s license within one year of hire.</li><li>Basic knowledge of horticulture and ornamental plant materials, including trees and utilizing the proper grounds operations equipment required to maintain their growth habits and needs.</li><li>Ability to identify common native landscape plants of Texas</li><li>Experience planting annuals</li></ul> <ul><li>Basic knowledge of proper pesticide use.</li><li>Knowledge of invasive plant species in our area.</li><li>Tree pruning experience</li></ul> <div>Assist the Director of Grounds in developing and maintaining a high-quality tier 1 landscape by performing quality assurance duties, identifying landscape improvement and renovation needs, assist in designing new beds, and identifying plant replacement needs. Ensure new landscape establishment.</div> <ul><li>Assist in preparing landscape beds by removing plant materials, amending soils, fertilizing, and mulching.</li><li>Assist installing landscape materials.</li><li>Assist in maintaining landscaped bed areas throughout campus. Perform quality assurance inspections and generate work orders.</li><li>Assist in preparation of special events.</li><li>Assist tree maintenance staff with tree planting, maintenance, or removal.</li><li>Assist in equipment preventative maintenance.</li><li>Identify herbicide application needs, plan and perform applications</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58266 2026-08-24T08:53:06-05:00 2026-08-24T08:53:07-05:00 GIS Technician <div>Texas State University is searching for a GIS Technician who can support the environmental compliance program at Fort Knox, located near Louisville, Kentucky. We are looking for a person who can provide technical guidance to the Government in performing data acquisition and analysis that is accurate, complete, current, and valid for the installation’s environmental layers. This includes coordinating with the government regarding implementation of the GIS program; strategic planning; compliance with federal, state, local, and Army Regulations, Directives, and Standards; providing technical support to the Government in the development of Standard Operating Procedures and management plans. This may also include providing technical input and recommendations regarding GIS operations, capabilities, and collection of data.</div><div><br>This position is located at Fort Knox, Kentucky, which is located just south of Louisville, Kentucky. Louisville is the largest city in Kentucky and is a cultural, entertainment, and sporting hub for the area. The primary objective of this position is to provide scientific and technical skills pertaining to the implementation of the Fort Knox air program. The job will involve a wide range of natural resource and environmental compliance projects that support military training and development.</div> Center for Archaeological Studies <ul><li>Successful completion of a four-year undergraduate degree in geography, GIS, an environmental discipline or related field from an accredited university or a GIS certificate from an accredited university. A combination of education and experience may be used in lieu of an accredited four-year undergraduate degree or certificate.</li><li>Demonstrated knowledge of ArcGIS Pro and Online or QGIS and associated mobile mapping products.</li><li>Demonstrated ability to develop and manage GIS data and databases.</li><li>Experience in using Microsoft Word, Excel, and databases for the development of supporting environmental analysis.</li><li>Ability to communicate effectively in formal briefings and in general public meetings, and to prepare clear and concise written materials appropriate for different audiences.</li></ul> <ul><li>Knowledge and use of Army GIS specifications.</li><li>Knowledge of relevant environmental, natural, and cultural resources processes at military installations and the integration with other environmental laws.</li><li>Ability to gather facts, analyze and compare trends, draw conclusions, devise solutions to problems, and identify changes and trends related to comprehensive planning issues.</li><li>Candidate must be able to work independently as well as part of a team that regularly interacts with military and civilian personnel and state and federal agencies.</li></ul> <div>Texas State University is searching for a GIS Technician who can support the environmental compliance program at Fort Knox, located near Louisville, Kentucky. We are looking for a person who can provide technical guidance to the Government in performing data acquisition and analysis that is accurate, complete, current, and valid for the installation’s environmental layers. This includes coordinating with the government regarding implementation of the GIS program; strategic planning; compliance with federal, state, local, and Army Regulations, Directives, and Standards; providing technical support to the Government in the development of Standard Operating Procedures and management plans. This may also include providing technical input and recommendations regarding GIS operations, capabilities, and collection of data.</div><div><br>This position is located at Fort Knox, Kentucky, which is located just south of Louisville, Kentucky. Louisville is the largest city in Kentucky and is a cultural, entertainment, and sporting hub for the area. The primary objective of this position is to provide scientific and technical skills pertaining to the implementation of the Fort Knox air program. The job will involve a wide range of natural resource and environmental compliance projects that support military training and development.</div> <div>GIS Data Development and Maintenance</div><div>Gather, update, maintain, and/or access all existing GIS data including:</div><div>Planimetric, utility, operations and security, master planning, environmental, cultural resources, and natural resources using the most recently available aerial photography, GPS field data collection and validation, hard-copy maps, as-built drawings, data conversion, and in-house knowledge.</div><div><br>Providing technical input to the Government in determining the most appropriate GIS workflow procedures including data format, storage, and maintenance. It may require projecting geographically un-projected data layers provided by outside entities such as the surrounding local governments and/or State or Federally available data.</div><div><br>Continue to develop, maintain, and make available metadata for all geospatial data maintained in the GIS database. This effort will provide another level of credibility to Ft Knox GIS data.</div><div>Current data layers to be updated on an annual basis: 41 Compliance layers and 12 Conservation layers.</div><div><br>Provide customized geodatabases that are created, implemented and supported within ESRI ArcGIS to meet the varied needs of installation staff and to support external units, agencies, and activities.<br><br>All geospatial data layer creation and updates shall conform to the established guidelines; be capable of being incorporated into the Installation GIS programs; comply with applicable security requirements; comply with the latest SDSFIE version, FGDC standards, &amp; IGI&amp;S guidelines to include current Quality Assurance Plans (QAP’s).</div><div><br>GIS Mapping and Analysis Support</div><div>Provide mapping and GIS analysis support to the Government. This includes: specialized GIS analysis including project specific GIS and/or GIS related data; specialized GIS analysis support, including interpretation and analysis of environmental data and development of natural resource support recommendations; and support to planning and siting studies, and environmental impact assessments.</div><div><br>Implement consistency of design across all GIS mapping products, including the utilization of standard symbology on mapping products, to sustain consistency with Federal agencies, DoD organizations.</div><div><br>GPS Support and Validation.</div><div>Provide GPS field data collection and validation support. Field data collection will be coordinated with the Government Tech Rep. Data collected will be post-processed, as needed, by the Partner prior to integration with the GIS.</div><div><br>If required, participate in meetings with agencies in support of GPS- related activities.</div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58261 2026-08-24T07:59:50-05:00 2026-08-24T07:59:52-05:00 Head Custodian <div>The Head Custodian position provides leadership, coordination, and supervision of custodial operations at Texas State Housing Facilities to ensure a clean and safe environment. The head custodian supervises full-time staff that service student residential facilities.</div> DHRL Administration <ul><li>High school graduation or GED.</li><li>Ability to communicate and understand verbal and written instructions in English.</li><li>Experience in working in any of the following: custodial, hospitality, environmental services, warehouse, production, or facilities maintenance.</li><li>Ability to lift, push, pull, and carry items weighing up to 30 lbs. unassisted and 50 pounds assisted.</li><li>Walk 3-5 miles daily and access all areas of the building in a timely manner.</li></ul> <ul><li>Experience supervising staff members.</li><li>Experience providing professional cleaning methods and techniques, including measuring and mixing cleaning chemicals.</li><li>Proficient with MS Word, Excel, and Outlook.</li><li>Bilingual, English &amp; Spanish.</li><li>Ability to provide excellent communication and interpersonal skills.</li></ul> <div>The Head Custodian position provides leadership, coordination, and supervision of custodial operations at Texas State Housing Facilities to ensure a clean and safe environment. The head custodian supervises full-time staff that service student residential facilities.</div> <div><strong>Custodial Services:</strong></div><ul><li>Directly supervise a custodial staff team and perform various cleaning duties such as sweeping, mopping, vacuuming, dusting, cleaning windows, and removing trash.</li><li>Provide floor care, including shampooing carpets, carpet extraction, using automatic scrubbers, and stripping and finishing floors.</li><li>Ensure that assigned facilities are maintained in a clean and safe condition&nbsp;</li></ul><div><strong>On-Call &amp; Emergency Management</strong></div><ul><li>Serve as a member of the departmental on-call rotation to provide support to students after hours.</li><li>Provide emergency response and clean up for floods and other custodial emergencies. Fill in as required for other crew members and substitute for absent co-workers as needed. Perform set-ups and breakdowns for special events.</li><li>Mandatory overtime may be required with little or no advance notice.</li><li>Other duties as assigned.&nbsp;</li></ul><div><strong>Administration:</strong></div><ul><li>Performs quality control inspections and documentation.</li><li>Manage staff performance through 1:1s, team meetings, and annual evaluations.</li><li>Process and review time reports, inspection reports, absence documentation.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58260 2026-08-24T07:57:17-05:00 2026-08-24T07:57:19-05:00 Locksmith <div>The locksmith will perform the work required to maintain, repair, install, and operate doors and locks of the mechanical and electronic variety to ensure the safety and security of the residence halls and apartments managed and operated by the Department of Housing and Residential Life.</div> DHRL Administration <ul><li>High School Diploma or GED.</li><li>Knowledge of lock and key mechanics, equipment, and systems.</li><li>Experience as a Locksmith or cutting keys.</li></ul> <ul><li>At least 1 year of experience installing, repairing, and maintaining commercial locks, automatic doors, exit devices, and other locking devices on all types of doors, gates, key watchers, and other equipment.</li><li>Experience with electronic key controls.</li><li>Performs installation, maintenance, inspection, modification, retrofitting, and repair of electronic locks, delayed egress devices, and Access Control systems.</li><li>Locksmith license of certification.</li><li>Demonstrated excellent interpersonal communication skills with the ability to receive, respond, and follow through with written and verbal work-related instructions and requests from supervisors, customers, and co-workers.</li></ul> <div>The locksmith will perform the work required to maintain, repair, install, and operate doors and locks of the mechanical and electronic variety to ensure the safety and security of the residence halls and apartments managed and operated by the Department of Housing and Residential Life.</div> <div><strong>Safety and Security:</strong></div><ul><li>Install, repair, and pin commercial cylinder cores to operate within an established master key system.</li><li>Use PDA to change lock codes as needed. Respond to emergencies to repair broken locks.</li><li>Analyze computer-generated work orders and prioritize repairs. Use troubleshooting and diagnostic techniques to perform maintenance, repairs, system identification, and equipment malfunctions. Work with key software.</li><li>Communicate with supervisor, staff, and residents. Complete and submit paperwork to your supervisor at the end of each day.</li><li>Ensure all inventory items are signed out and accounted for daily. Sign and close out all completed work orders daily with a description of the work performed.</li><li>Serve as part of the call rotations for after-hours emergencies.</li></ul><div><strong>Special Projects:</strong></div><ul><li>Assisted in installing and repairing door access systems, including door management alarms, card readers, electric strikes, electrified exit devices, delayed egress devices, and door contacts.</li><li>Transport equipment and supplies as needed to perform routine preventive maintenance and/or repairs.</li><li>Promote professional development of self and all staff to improve knowledge and skills through ongoing training and workshops, including monthly safety training.</li><li>Other related functions as assigned.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58242 2026-08-21T07:54:28-05:00 2026-08-21T07:54:29-05:00 HR Business Partner <div>Responsible for aligning business objectives with HR strategies/services<br>by serving as a consultant to leadership and employees. Acts as a<br>liaison between supported divisions/departments and HR specialty<br>functions to ensure that HR solutions are aligned with institutional<br>priorities.</div> Human Resources <div><strong>Required Qualifications</strong><br>Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the following qualifications:</div><ul><li>Bachelor’s degree in human resource management, Organizational Development, Business Administration or related field.</li><li>A minimum of three (3) years of Human Resources experience providing guidance and consultation to internal customers/business managers on employee relations and performance management, with exposure to working with compensation, talent acquisition, learning/development, organizational development, benefits, and HRIS is required.</li><li>Knowledge of federal and state employment laws and HR best practices.</li><li>Understanding of core human resources functions including employee relations, talent acquisition, compensation, organizational development, performance management, learning and development, HRIS, and employee engagement.</li><li>Experience using HR systems, data management tools, and technology to support HR operations and decision-making.</li><li>Strong relationship-building, consulting, and communication skills with the ability to effectively partner with leaders and employees at all levels.</li><li>Demonstrated critical thinking, problem-solving, conflict resolution, and decision-making abilities.</li><li>Ability to analyze and interpret workforce data, trends, and metrics to support business and organizational objectives.</li><li>Experience managing multiple priorities and providing strategic HR guidance in a fast-paced environment.</li><li>Ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, and proactively identify and address organizational needs.</li><li>Strong collaboration skills with the ability to build effective partnerships across departments and HR functional areas.</li><li>Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, HR systems, and other digital tools, including emerging AI technologies.</li></ul> <div><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></div><ul><li>Master’s degree in human resources, Business Administration, Organizational Development, or a related field.</li><li>Professional HR certification (PHR, SPHR, SHRM-CP, SHRM-SCP, or equivalent).</li><li>Previous experience in higher education or a public-sector environment.</li></ul> <div>Responsible for aligning business objectives with HR strategies/services<br>by serving as a consultant to leadership and employees. Acts as a<br>liaison between supported divisions/departments and HR specialty<br>functions to ensure that HR solutions are aligned with institutional<br>priorities.</div> <div><strong>Duties</strong></div><ul><li>Manage and resolve complex employee relations matters and workplace concerns with professionalism, sound judgment, and a solutions-oriented approach.</li><li>Provide day-to-day guidance and coaching to managers related to performance management, employee development, disciplinary actions, and workplace issues.</li><li>Partner closely with leadership and employees to foster positive working relationships, strengthen employee engagement, and support productivity and retention efforts.</li><li>Advise departments on HR policies, procedures, and best practices while identifying opportunities for process improvement and operational effectiveness.</li><li>Participate in regular meetings with division and department leadership to provide strategic HR consultation and support.</li><li>Support organizational initiatives including workforce planning, succession planning, departmental restructures, and talent management strategies.</li><li>Collaborate with Compensation and Classification teams on position reviews, updates, and compensation-related considerations to ensure alignment with institutional practices and market standards.</li><li>Partner with Talent Acquisition on recruitment strategies, key searches, and hiring initiatives to attract and retain top talent.</li><li>Identify learning and development opportunities for departments and leaders and collaborate with HR partners to support training and coaching initiatives.</li><li>Analyze workforce trends, metrics, and organizational data to recommend HR solutions, programs, and process improvements.</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58224 2026-08-19T12:57:50-05:00 2026-08-19T12:57:53-05:00 PRN Certified Medical Assistant <div>Join the Texas State University Student Health Center, a nationally accredited ambulatory health care facility with in-house laboratory and radiology services. Serving more than 40,000 students, our team-oriented organization is committed to providing high-quality, patient-centered care. We are seeking a <strong>PRN Medical Assistant</strong> to become part of our dedicated clinical team. Clinic operating hours are Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.<br><br></div> University Health Services <ul><li>Completion of accredited Medical Assistant program</li><li>Certified Medical Assistant</li><li>Computer experience including use of Microsoft Office</li><li>Experience documenting in electronic health records</li><li>Experience working in a Primary Care clinic (Family Medicine or Internal Medicine) or an Urgent Care clinic.</li></ul> <ul><li>Experience using eClinical Works.</li><li>Current Basic Life Support (BLS) certificate</li></ul> <div>Join the Texas State University Student Health Center, a nationally accredited ambulatory health care facility with in-house laboratory and radiology services. Serving more than 40,000 students, our team-oriented organization is committed to providing high-quality, patient-centered care. We are seeking a <strong>PRN Medical Assistant</strong> to become part of our dedicated clinical team. Clinic operating hours are Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.<br><br></div> <div><strong>Front &amp; Back Office Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>Obtain and document patient history, vital signs, allergies, and chief complaints.</li><li>Schedule appointments and maintain accurate electronic medical records.</li><li>Perform clinical procedures, including EKGs, wound care, immunizations, and medication administration.</li><li>Assist providers during examinations and procedures; coordinate referrals and follow-up care.</li><li>Prepare and stock exam rooms, label specimens, and maintain clinical supplies.</li><li>Ensure accurate documentation and compliance with safety and infection-control standards.</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58210 2026-08-18T09:55:25-05:00 2026-08-18T09:55:26-05:00 Senior Proposal Coordinator <div>Senior Proposal Coordinator is responsible for coordinating all aspects of compliance verification, review, and submission of grant proposals as well as conducting the final institutional review and clearance.</div> Pre-Award Sponsored Programs <ul><li>At least two years of experience in proposal review, including budgets.</li><li>Knowledge of applicable federal and state regulations--including compliance areas (effort, human subjects, export control, national security)—and various funding source requirements (such as NIH, NSF, DOE, DoD, USDA/NIFA, foundation, and industry sponsors), and ability to interpret and explain complex regulations.</li><li>Familiarity with electronic submission portals (e.g., Grants.gov, E-Grants, Tex-grants, Research.gov).</li><li>Demonstrated communication, customer service, conflict resolution, teamwork, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to navigate challenging situations professionally.</li><li>Demonstrated ability to manage complex projects involving multiple stakeholders, competing priorities, and strict deadlines.</li><li>Bachelor’s degree&nbsp;</li></ul> <ul><li>Certified Research Administrator (CRA), Certified Pre-Award Research Administrator (CPRA), or willingness to achieve certification.</li><li>Experience with Kuali, Cayuse, SAP, Workday or other finance or research administration software<strong>.</strong></li><li>At least four years of research administration or sponsored programs experience, particularly in a university setting.</li><li>Advanced Excel skills, Planner, Power Automate, or AI tools.</li><li>Knowledge of university policies and procedures.</li></ul> <div>Senior Proposal Coordinator is responsible for coordinating all aspects of compliance verification, review, and submission of grant proposals as well as conducting the final institutional review and clearance.</div> <div><strong>Senior Proposal Coordinator</strong></div><div>The Senior Proposal Coordinator serves as the institutional review authority for sponsored proposals and is responsible for coordinating proposal review, compliance verification, and submission activities in accordance with university policies and sponsor requirements.</div><div><strong>Proposal Review &amp; Submission</strong></div><div>Review, coordinate, and submit grant proposals and related documents for federal, state, foundation, and other sponsors. Conduct final institutional review to ensure proposals are complete, accurate, and compliant with sponsor requirements and university policies. Verify required approvals, certifications, budgets, and supporting documentation prior to submission.</div><div><strong>Proposal Coordination &amp; Project Management</strong></div><div>Monitor proposal pipelines, deadlines, and submission activities. Work closely with Research Coordinators, faculty, and administrative staff to facilitate timely proposal preparation and submission. Identify issues that may affect submission timelines and assist in resolving them.</div><div><strong>Compliance &amp; Risk Review</strong></div><div>Ensure adherence to sponsor guidelines, university policies, and applicable regulations. Review budgets, cost sharing, F&amp;A rates, subrecipient documentation, and other proposal components for compliance. Escalate complex compliance or policy issues to appropriate offices and leadership.</div><div><strong>Sponsor &amp; Institutional Liaison Support</strong></div><div>Communicate with sponsors, collaborating institutions, and internal stakeholders regarding proposal requirements, submission processes, and administrative matters. Coordinate with other university offices as needed to support proposal development and review.</div><div><strong>Customer Service &amp; Communication</strong></div><div>Provide responsive support and guidance to faculty, staff, and colleagues regarding proposal preparation, sponsor requirements, and submission procedures. Promote collaborative working relationships and a high level of customer service.</div><div><strong>Training &amp; Operational Support</strong></div><div>Assist with updating procedures, forms, and guidance materials. Support onboarding, mentoring, and training of new staff. Contribute to special projects, reporting activities, and continuous improvement efforts within the office.</div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58169 2026-08-12T10:02:04-05:00 2026-08-12T10:02:05-05:00 Administrative Assistant III <div>The Administrative Assistant III provides administrative and clerical support to program chairs, department chairs, deans, or directors within their specific departments.</div> Office of Educator Preparation <ul><li>Knowledge of university/academic policies and procedures.</li><li>Advanced working knowledge of Microsoft Office, spreadsheets, databases, and other desktop software.</li><li>Experience prioritizing workload and completing assignments with tight deadlines.</li><li>Experience with budget and PCRs, including using software such as SAP (GUI, Marketplace, Concur) or similar.</li><li>Experience working with university GATO website management, including CALICO.</li><li>Knowledge of Student information systems such as Ellucian Banner 9, Degree works, Navigate, SL&amp;L or similar.</li><li>Ability to work as a team member and interact appropriately with others.</li><li>Must be a current Texas State Employee</li></ul> <ul><li>Bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience level.</li><li>Previous university experience</li></ul> <div>The Administrative Assistant III provides administrative and clerical support to program chairs, department chairs, deans, or directors within their specific departments.</div> <ul><li>Manage hiring and processing PCRs and stipend requests.</li><li>Monitor and process time management for the department's staff.</li><li>Monitor transactions within the operating budget and maintain precise ledgers.</li><li>Review and process purchase orders and invoices.</li><li>Coordinate travel arrangements, applications, and reimbursements for all staff.</li><li>Serve as support to the front office to greet, screen, and route customers</li><li>Assist with the department's general email.</li><li>Use independent judgment to effectively prioritize workload while working in a team-oriented, customer service-based environment.</li><li>Coordinate and oversee the supervisor's calendar and schedule.</li><li>Organize, prioritize, direct, and explain office work assignments to office staff and student workers.</li><li>Provide training for admin II and student workers.</li><li>Manage the office facilities and supplies.</li><li>Assist in the preparation of various activities and events.</li><li>Support Admin Asst II with student registration.</li><li>Ensure compliance with state educator preparation requirements within the workflow of the department's staff.</li><li>Maintain compliant log and organize student appeals for review.</li><li>Collaborate to provide insight on process improvements and successful outcomes.</li><li>Responsible for updating content and managing GATO for the department website.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58124 2026-08-06T12:42:55-05:00 2026-08-06T12:42:58-05:00 PRN LVN Nurse Pool <div>Texas State University Health Services is seeking a <strong>PRN</strong> <strong>Licensed Vocational Nurse (LVN) </strong>to assist physician or nurse practitioner at its ambulatory health care facility serving college students<strong>. </strong>Responsible for providing nursing care, treatment, and health education for Texas State students.</div> University Health Services <ul><li>Current LVN license in good standing issued by the state of Texas or by Nurse Licensure Compact Administration.</li><li>Minimum of one year of LVN experience working in a clinical setting with direct patient care duties.</li><li>Experience documenting in electronic medical records systems.</li></ul> <ul><li>Direct patient care nursing experience in a family practice, internal medicine, pediatrics, hospital emergency department or college health setting within the last 5 years.</li><li>Experience documenting in eClinical Works</li><li>Current BLS or ACLS certification.</li></ul> <div>Texas State University Health Services is seeking a <strong>PRN</strong> <strong>Licensed Vocational Nurse (LVN) </strong>to assist physician or nurse practitioner at its ambulatory health care facility serving college students<strong>. </strong>Responsible for providing nursing care, treatment, and health education for Texas State students.</div> <div>Responsibilities include nursing care of patients in an outpatient primary care setting that includes general medicine, women’s health, sports medicine, urgent care and mental health services. Licensed Vocational Nurses (LVN) assist a team of medical providers with patient treatments, office procedures, patient follow-up, prescription refills, telephone messages and other duties as assigned.</div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58081 2026-08-03T15:42:18-05:00 2026-08-03T15:42:20-05:00 Public Safety Sergeant <div>Responsible for supervising public safety officers while enforcing the parking regulations of the university, assisting motorists, and securing the safety of students, faculty, and staff. <strong>This is a night shift position.</strong></div> Security/Parking Operations <ul><li>High School Diploma or Equivalent.</li><li>Experience in supervising public safety officers, to include report and citation review and approval, security systems management, fleet management, and personnel matters.</li><li>Ability to understand policies and procedures.</li><li>Manage public safety officer training program.</li><li>Must be able to complete CPR, First Aid, AED, Naloxone, and CJIS certification is required upon one (1) year of employment.</li><li>Must turn in a personal history statement and be able to pass a full background.</li></ul> <ul><li>Prior public safety officer experience in the state of Texas or out of state equivalent.</li><li>Some college education preferred, ideally in the criminology or criminal justice fields.</li><li>Demonstrated outstanding organizational skills; attention to detail; ability to work under minimal supervision; evidence of initiative and proactive approach to solving problems. .</li><li>Demonstrated ability to quickly learn new procedures and to problem-solve independently; excellent written and oral communication skills.</li><li>Able to read, write and speak English</li><li>Good physical condition, able to walk and/or stand for long periods</li><li>Acceptable driving record and eligible to operate a university-owned vehicle in accordance with university policy.</li><li>Criminal record free of felony convictions, good credit, stable employment history</li></ul> <div>Responsible for supervising public safety officers while enforcing the parking regulations of the university, assisting motorists, and securing the safety of students, faculty, and staff. <strong>This is a night shift position.</strong></div> <ul><li>Respond to calls for service.</li><li>Operate a patrol vehicle.</li><li>Assist motorists.</li><li>Attend shift briefings.</li><li>Supervise public safety officers, including report and citation review and approval, security systems management, fleet management, and personnel matters.</li><li>Support department outreach and engagement efforts.</li><li>Oversee the Emergency Call Box system through regular audits.</li><li>Manage shift schedules and assign appropriate shifts.</li><li>Collaborate with campus partners requiring security services.</li><li>Conduct regular assessments of campus security camera systems.</li><li>Understand policies and procedures; provide excellent customer service; manage public safety officer training program.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58065 2026-08-03T08:11:45-05:00 2026-08-03T08:11:46-05:00 Head Plumber <div>Responsible for providing emergency response to maintenance oriented calls or plumbing emergencies across all campus facilities.&nbsp;</div> Facilities Operations <ul><li>Valid Texas Journeyman [or higher] Plumber license</li><li>Valid Backflow license or be able to obtain one in 180 days</li><li>Plumbing experience and knowledge of plumbing concepts, codes and laws; EPA regulations, safety procedures and regulations; repair and maintenance of all types of plumbing fixtures and their apparatus.</li><li>Experience working independently and as part of a team troubleshooting and correcting plumbing challenges, including emergency responses.</li><li>Available and willing to work after-hours on-call duty, on a rotating basis with other shop personnel</li></ul> <ul><li>Master Plumber license</li><li>Previous employment experience as a plumber (or equivalent) in government and/or higher education environment</li><li>Experience with AiM (Assetworks) Integrated Work Management System</li></ul> <div>Responsible for providing emergency response to maintenance oriented calls or plumbing emergencies across all campus facilities.&nbsp;</div> <ul><li>Maintain and operate heavy equipment.<br>Repair water and sewer lines pumps, faucets, water closets, tubs, showers, water heaters on emergency basis, as needed.</li><li>Train and mentor other plumbing shop personnel</li><li>Unstop clogged water closets, urinals, sinks, bathtubs, shower and floor drains, and sewers; repair water, gas, and sewer lines; repair/replace laboratory faucets, traps, and sinks; and repair/replace hose bibs; and test and repair backflow devices. Unclog storm and roof drains.</li><li>Repair, replace, varied plumbing fixtures on campus. Construct, remove or rough-in fixtures in varied campus bldg., properties.</li><li>Install or maintain various water, gas, air, sewer, as needed, at various campus facilities.</li><li>Complete daily mileage, work logs and requisition parts, materials, personnel.</li><li>Complete electronic work logs and requisition parts, materials, personnel.</li><li>Complies with all state and university policies.</li><li>Works various schedules and required to be on call.</li><li>Required to carry a cell phone.</li><li>Operate a university vehicle.</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58008 2026-07-28T14:39:45-05:00 2026-07-28T14:39:47-05:00 Locksmith <div>Responsible for installing, repairing, rekeying, and maintaining all locks on campus. Responsible for installing, repairing, rekeying, and maintaining all locks on campus.</div> Facilities Services <ul><li>Must possess mechanical knowledge of lock/key equipment and systems</li><li>Experience cutting keys</li><li>Experience auditing and maintaining inventory</li><li>Must be available and willing to work after-hours on-call duty, on a rotating basis with other shop personnel</li></ul> <ul><li>At least one (1) year of professional experience in this trade</li><li>Experience in higher education and/or government</li><li>Proficiency using e-mail and portable electronic communication devices</li><li>Experience using AiM (AssetWorks)</li></ul><div><br></div> <div>Responsible for installing, repairing, rekeying, and maintaining all locks on campus. Responsible for installing, repairing, rekeying, and maintaining all locks on campus.</div> <ul><li>Maintains, repairs, removes, and installs cores and locks in all university buildings. Install or repair entry dead bolts, combination locks, and desk and file cabinet locks.</li><li>Install and/or repair panic bars on all campus buildings. Repair and adjust door closers.</li><li>Maintain and operate key-cutting machines.</li><li>Cuts and issues keys for all buildings offices, dorm rooms, vehicles, file cabinets, and desks.</li><li>Keeps record of issued keys. Searches through key data system to identify key holders and keys assigned.</li><li>Maintain key catalog system for all campus buildings.</li><li>Identify lost keys and return them to the appropriate department.</li><li>Install security plates.</li><li>Keep and update keys for university vehicles and loan vehicles.</li><li>Check all locks in new buildings to ensure correct operation.</li><li>Perform routine preventative maintenance.</li><li>Works various schedules and is required to be on call.</li><li>Required to carry a cell phone.</li><li>Operates university vehicle.</li><li>Complies with all state and university policies.</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57981 2026-07-27T07:56:14-05:00 2026-07-27T07:56:15-05:00 Plant Operator II <div>Responsible for providing safe, reliable, electrical power, chilled water and steam in a timely and responsive manner to meet the needs of the university.</div> Facilities Services <ul><li>Knowledge of intermediate theory and practice of electro-mechanical equipment for operation, computer automation software including INSIGHT, DESIGO, IoT, and BACnet protocols.</li><li>Ability to analyze and identify equipment problems and troubleshoot electrical and hydraulic system issues.</li><li>Experience using computer programs such as MS Office.</li><li>Strong Interpersonal Skills.</li><li>Knowledge of the manual and computerized maintenance and operation of chillers, chilled water production, steam boilers, heat exchangers, steam production, and feed water systems.</li><li>Ability to obtain certification for operating forklifts, genie booms, and scissor lifts through university training.</li></ul> <ul><li>Experience with various types of electric energy generation.</li><li>Experience with electrical and pneumatic controls.</li><li>Experience taking telephone messages and managing communication effectively.</li><li>General Knowledge of electric power systems, grids, generation, transmission, distribution; blue prints and one-line diagrams.</li></ul><div><br></div> <div>Responsible for providing safe, reliable, electrical power, chilled water and steam in a timely and responsive manner to meet the needs of the university.</div> <ul><li>Use computer terminals to monitor, control and command equipment in all thermal plants.</li><li>Lead Plant Operator I to physically ensure all equipment is available and prepared to start / stop and to support automated operation of equipment.</li><li>Prepare and complete log sheets, update daily logs and monthly reports for chill water, steam production and water consumption.</li><li>Watch, test, and troubleshoot chemical stations and monitor water chemical levels for equipment protection and energy efficiency.</li><li>Operate, inspect, report, clean, paint, repair, and maintain electromechanical equipment in all campus plants.</li><li>Serve as the point of contact for the University Contact Center and direct business and after-hour phone calls to proper shops for assistance.</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned.</li></ul><div><br></div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57980 2026-07-27T07:54:21-05:00 2026-07-27T07:54:22-05:00 Habitat Conservation Tech <div>The Habitat Conservation Technician helps protect some of the University’s most sensitive and valuable resources, its tree canopy. Monitoring the health and safety of Texas State University’s tree canopy, performing hazard and risk assessments for both pedestrian traffic and property. Maintain our tree inventory identifying replacement needs as trees are removed for construction, health, or risk. Research, design, plan, and perform duties in the prevention, control, and remediation of invasive species using various disciplines and industry accepted best management practices. Sustainably improve, manage, and protect Texas State University’s landscape natural resources creating a comfortable and safe environment in which to learn.</div> Facilities Services <ul><li>Ability to communicate, receive and assign instructions, direct work, recognize and change priorities. Good oral and written communication skills.</li><li>Ability to determine acceptable work quality and quantity.</li><li>Ability to work independently and in a team environment to handle complex projects, prioritize and manage multiple tasks under deadlines.</li><li>Ability to lift and carry items weighing up to 50 lbs., and perform strenuous physical duties for an entire shift.</li><li>Ability to work outdoors in extreme and varying weather conditions.</li><li>Ability to operate industry equipment for extended periods.</li><li>Knowledge and application of safety practices related to job duties, and safe use of industry related equipment.</li><li>Ability to perform Job Hazard Analysis.</li><li>A commitment to quality, customer service, personal development and safety.</li><li>Must have two years of tree pruning experience</li><li>Must be able to attain ISA arborist certification within one year of hire.</li><li>Must be able to attain TDA pesticide applicator’s license within one year of hire.</li></ul> <ul><li>Basic knowledge of horticulture and ornamental plant materials, including trees and utilizing the proper grounds operations equipment required to maintain their growth habits and needs.</li><li>Basic knowledge of proper pesticide use.</li><li>Knowledge of invasive plant species in our area.</li></ul> <div>The Habitat Conservation Technician helps protect some of the University’s most sensitive and valuable resources, its tree canopy. Monitoring the health and safety of Texas State University’s tree canopy, performing hazard and risk assessments for both pedestrian traffic and property. Maintain our tree inventory identifying replacement needs as trees are removed for construction, health, or risk. Research, design, plan, and perform duties in the prevention, control, and remediation of invasive species using various disciplines and industry accepted best management practices. Sustainably improve, manage, and protect Texas State University’s landscape natural resources creating a comfortable and safe environment in which to learn.</div> <div>The Habitat Conservation Technician’s duties include monitoring the health of Texas State University’s tree canopy and potential tree hazards on campus. Perform pruning of immature trees to guide growth, reducing future potential hazards and improving aesthetic form. Perform pruning for safe visibility, line of sight and lighting clearance. Monitor and maintain invasive species on campus properties. Plan and host Arbor Day events and other arboriculture educational opportunities. Maintain the University’s tree inventory, updating removals and additions.</div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57979 2026-07-27T07:51:23-05:00 2026-07-27T07:51:24-05:00 Locksmith <div>Responsible for installing, repairing, rekeying, and maintaining all locks on campus. Responsible for installing, repairing, rekeying, and maintaining all locks on campus.</div> Facilities Services <ul><li>Must possess mechanical knowledge of lock/key equipment and systems</li><li>Experience cutting keys</li><li>Experience auditing and maintaining inventory</li><li>Must be available and willing to work after-hours on-call duty, on a rotating basis with other shop personnel</li></ul> <ul><li>At least one (1) year of professional experience in this trade</li><li>Experience in higher education and/or government</li><li>Proficiency using e-mail and portable electronic communication devices</li><li>Experience using AiM (AssetWorks)</li></ul> <div>Responsible for installing, repairing, rekeying, and maintaining all locks on campus. Responsible for installing, repairing, rekeying, and maintaining all locks on campus.</div> <ul><li>Maintains, repairs, removes, and installs cores and locks in all university buildings. Install or repair entry dead bolts, combination locks, and desk and file cabinet locks.</li><li>Install and/or repair panic bars on all campus buildings. Repair and adjust door closers.</li><li>Maintain and operate key-cutting machines.</li><li>Cuts and issues keys for all buildings offices, dorm rooms, vehicles, file cabinets, and desks.</li><li>Keep record of issued keys. Searches through key data system to identify key holders and keys assigned.</li><li>Maintain key catalog system for all campus buildings.</li><li>Identify lost keys and return them to the appropriate department.</li><li>Install security plates.</li><li>Keep and update keys for university vehicles and loan vehicles.</li><li>Check all locks in new buildings to ensure correct operation.</li><li>Perform routine preventative maintenance.</li><li>Works various schedules and is required to be on call.</li><li>Required to carry a cell phone.</li><li>Complies with all state and university policies.</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57977 2026-07-27T07:44:37-05:00 2026-07-27T07:44:38-05:00 Electrician II <div>Perform journey-level electrical work including installation, maintenance, and repair of campus electrical systems and equipment.</div> Facilities Services <ul><li>Valid Texas Journeyman Electrician License.</li><li>Knowledge of National Electrical Code and applicable laws, construction standards, mechanical concepts, and electrical systems and circuitry.</li><li>Skill in troubleshooting electrical equipment and diagnosing problems in circuitry.</li><li>Skill in use of trade equipment, tools, and calculations, including formulae, voltage, resistance, amperage, wattage, etc.</li><li>Willing to work after-hours on-call duty on a rotating basis with Round Rock shop personnel</li></ul> <ul><li>Previous employment experience as an electrician or similar in government and/or higher education environment</li><li>Proficiency managing work orders using a portable electronic tablet/device</li><li>Use of AiM (AssetWorks)</li></ul> <div>Perform journey-level electrical work including installation, maintenance, and repair of campus electrical systems and equipment.</div> <ul><li>Work performed includes performing all electrical work assignments, including lighting and PMs, on the Texas State University Round Rock campus.</li><li>Assist w/ special event setups.</li><li>Assist w/ furniture moves.</li><li>Help identify irrigation problems and report back to supervisor.</li><li>Perform PMs and light repairs at the CUB.</li><li>Participate in on-call rotation for the Round Rock Facilities group.</li><li>Identify, remove, and replace inoperative lamps, ballasts, lamp holders, switches, fixtures, receptacles, breakers, panels, and switchgears.</li><li>Troubleshoot, repair, replace, and perform preventative maintenance on electrical equipment.</li><li>Restore electricity to buildings or equipment by identifying the reason for outage, rerouting power and making necessary repairs.</li><li>Analyze and repair or replace receptacles, circuit breakers, panel boards, switch gear, motor starters, and wiring connections.</li><li>Provide technical support at sporting and other special events.</li><li>Perform routine housekeeping duties in the shop area, and equipment rooms.</li><li>Reset power supply during malfunctions.</li><li>Install conduit, boxes, fittings, and electrical equipment and pull wire for circuits.</li><li>Time keeping, part ordering, and database research.</li><li>Works various schedules and is required to be on call.</li><li>Required to carry a cell phone.</li><li>Operate university vehicle.</li><li>Complies with all state and university policies.</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57920 2026-07-22T07:54:44-05:00 2026-07-22T07:54:46-05:00 Fire Protection Head Controls Technician <div>Provide technical leadership and operational support for the campus Fire Protection Systems. This position guides and trains Controls Technicians I and II, assists with planning and prioritizing daily work, coordinates with contractors and vendors, and supports the Supervisor in maintaining reliable fire protection monitoring, response, inspection, testing, maintenance, and repair operations.<br><br></div><div>The primary focus of this position is campus Fire Protection Systems. Fire suppression responsibilities are limited to related monitoring points, system interfaces, project coordination, and other duties, as assigned.<br><br></div> Facilities Operations <ul><li>Ability to assist with planning, prioritizing, and coordinating daily operations in support of the Supervisor, including Purchase Requests and Budget oversight.</li><li>Ability to guide and train staff in the installation, maintenance, programming, troubleshooting, and repair of campus fire protection systems, FireWorks, all in accordance with current NFPA Standards.</li><li>Ability to coordinate with Fire Marshal/AHJ, and Contractors performing Fire Protection inspections, repairs, upgrades, and project work, including deficiencies with Annual Inspection</li><li>Reports and reviewing project documentation for compliance with NFPA and Campus Construction Standards.</li><li>Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing.</li><li>Ability to work well with diverse groups and individuals and motivate them to produce required work outcomes.</li><li>Ability to use FireWorks to monitor all building Fire Protection Systems.</li><li>Ability to respond to and coordinate resolution of Fire Protection issues during on-call assignments.</li><li>Available and willing to work after-hours on-call duty, on a rotating basis with other shop personnel</li><li>Must have attended and passed Factory Training, by Edwards Systems Technologies, for EST3</li><li>Must have attended and passed Factory Training, by Edwards Systems Technologies, for FireWork</li></ul><div><br></div> <ul><li>Ability to prepare reports, spreadsheets, and summaries using operational data.</li><li>Experience using Microsoft Office and Work Order Management systems such as AiM.</li><li>Experience working with AutoCAD.</li><li>Experience with fire suppression system monitoring, supervisory signals, and related Fire Protection system interfaces.</li></ul><div><br></div> <div>Provide technical leadership and operational support for the campus Fire Protection Systems. This position guides and trains Controls Technicians I and II, assists with planning and prioritizing daily work, coordinates with contractors and vendors, and supports the Supervisor in maintaining reliable fire protection monitoring, response, inspection, testing, maintenance, and repair operations.<br><br></div><div>The primary focus of this position is campus Fire Protection Systems. Fire suppression responsibilities are limited to related monitoring points, system interfaces, project coordination, and other duties, as assigned.<br><br></div> <ul><li>Assist the Supervisor with planning, prioritizing, and coordinating daily Fire Protection operations.</li><li>Provide day-to-day leadership, guidance, and training to Controls Technicians I and II.</li><li>Coordinate Fire Protection work performed by staff, contractors, and vendors.</li><li>Support reliable operation of campus Fire Protection monitoring, response, inspection, testing, maintenance, and repair activities.</li><li>Review Fire Protection issues and assist with troubleshooting, corrective actions, and escalation as needed.</li><li>Support Fire Protection design reviews, renovations, projects, acceptance testing, and system turnover.</li><li>Support Fire Suppression monitoring points, supervisory signals, and Fire Protection system interfaces as needed.</li><li>Participate in the regular rotation of on-call duties.</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned.</li></ul><div><br></div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57895 2026-07-21T08:21:43-05:00 2026-07-21T08:21:44-05:00 Police Officer <div>Texas State University (TXST) Police Department is looking for lateral transfers who are motivated to help others and be a part of the UPD Team. Every day our officers work with students, faculty, staff and the community to ensure safety for everyone. Here at TXST University we are committed to having a diverse workforce that resembles the people of Texas and the University we serve.</div> Patrol Operations <ul><li>High School Diploma or equivalent.</li><li>Be licensed by TCOLE; or be a certified or licensed out of state peace officer and successfully obtain TCOLE licensing (basic peace officer or higher) within 90 days of hire.</li><li>Must have at least 1-year prior work experience as a full-time commissioned peace officer with similar duties in a comparable law enforcement agency.</li><li>Left previous agency with an honorable discharge.</li></ul><div><br></div> <ul><li>60 College Credit Hours / Associate’s Degree.</li><li>Bachelor’s Degree.</li><li>Previous work experience in university policing.</li><li>TCOLE Proficiency Certificate above Basic Peace Officer.</li><li>Current Full Time Working Peace Officer.</li></ul><div><br></div> <div>Texas State University (TXST) Police Department is looking for lateral transfers who are motivated to help others and be a part of the UPD Team. Every day our officers work with students, faculty, staff and the community to ensure safety for everyone. Here at TXST University we are committed to having a diverse workforce that resembles the people of Texas and the University we serve.</div> <ul><li>Enforcement of all laws of the State of Texas to include laws and ordinances for TXST University and the city of San Marcos.</li><li>Respond to emergency calls, traffic accidents and general requests for assistance.</li><li>Patrols university property to include campuses and leased properties.</li><li>Issues warnings and citations to violators of university, city and state regulations.</li><li>Conduct preliminary investigations into minor traffic crashes and crimes.</li><li>Writes offense, incident, arrest and impoundment reports in a timely manner.</li><li>Proper use of communication and recording equipment.</li><li>Appears in court and testifies under oath.</li><li>Performs special assignments as required, such as university events, investigations and parking enforcement or crime prevention.</li><li>Work 12-hour shifts, including nights, weekends and holidays.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57830 2026-07-16T08:43:51-05:00 2026-07-16T08:43:52-05:00 Supervisor, Grounds Operations <div>Responsible for supervising crews in the provision of an attractive, safe, and well maintained landscape by the use of tools and machinery.</div> Facilities Services <ul><li>Cultural management of turf and plant materials</li><li>Landscape maintenance equipment guidelines.</li><li>Policies, and laws related to chemical usage; usage of materials, equipment, and tools related to grounds maintenance.</li><li>Safety practices and procedures related to grounds maintenance including OSHA and SDS information.</li><li>Supervising staff of 3 or more and interacting with others departments; addressing customer concerns.</li><li>Effectively directing the work of others and motivate output.</li><li>Prioritizing workload; problem solving and decision making.</li><li>Read and understand technical materials, laws and regulations, and chemical labels.</li><li>Maintain records; complete work orders, process purchase requests, monitor shop budget.</li><li>Ability to communicate effectively</li><li>Ability to prioritize and schedule work.</li><li>Perform basic math; use measuring devices; review time sheets, interpret policies and procedures to staff, and communicate concerns to management.</li><li>Prepare and conduct training for staff; establish and maintain a filing system.</li><li>Hold a Texas Department of Agriculture-Pesticide Applicators License</li><li>Over 3 years of supervising employees&nbsp;</li></ul><div><br></div> <ul><li>Experience with hiring, promoting and disciplinary actions of staff.</li><li>Experience with committee participation.</li></ul> <div>Responsible for supervising crews in the provision of an attractive, safe, and well maintained landscape by the use of tools and machinery.</div> <ul><li>Responsible for supervising mowing/beds crew in daily maintenance of campus turf/beds areas and litter control.</li><li>Daily inspection of campus to identify campus landscape needs. Schedule/prioritize weekly, monthly, and long-range work including routine work and special events.</li><li>Provide crews with clear and specific assigned duties.</li><li>Provide quality control of staff performance.</li><li>Monitor and Manage employee time.</li><li>Ensure that all employees are properly trained in all aspects of normal duties, and all employees attend required training.</li><li>Provide Safety training.</li><li>Identify safety hazards and mitigate or inform appropriate shops.</li><li>Manage resources used to maintain grounds in an efficient, effective, and professional manner.</li><li>Provide employees with needed materials, equipment, and PPE.</li><li>Map, database, describe, and locate irrigation systems and ground areas using computer and GIS software.</li><li>Help maintain turf/beds by mowing, trimming, fertilizing, weeding, pruning, applying pesticides, monitoring irrigation.</li><li>Inspect grounds/irrigation systems and work in progress.</li><li>General clean up and preparation of campus for events, move-in, move-out, commencement,</li><li>football, tailgating, and other events, before and after.</li><li>Create work orders and assign them to staff.</li><li>Assist other crews to help with workload.</li><li>Help staff with computer data entry, time entry, Performance Management.</li><li>Schedule vehicles and equipment repairs with the garage and outside vendors.</li><li>Make pesticide applications.</li><li>Maintain Pesticide Applicator’s license.</li><li>Maintain TDA applicator records.</li><li>Coordinate with outside vendors/contractors.</li><li>Locate/contact potential vendors/contractors.</li><li>Coordinate work with other shops.</li><li>Coordinate work with other departments on campus.</li><li>Track work hours, chemical use, and other items.</li><li>Order equipment, supplies, and material needs.</li><li>Schedule irrigation.</li><li>Support crews in their work with materials, personnel needs, and special requests.</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned</li></ul><div><br></div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57795 2026-07-14T08:09:05-05:00 2026-07-14T08:09:06-05:00 Prospect Development Associate <div>Are you passionate about higher education accessibility? Do you enjoy detail-oriented work and being a part of a collaborative team? If so, the Prospect Development Associate role may just be the perfect opportunity for you to join the team at Texas State University.</div><div>The Prospect Development Associate position plays a vital role in sustaining the mission of the University Advancement division. The Associate is responsible for identifying and gathering intel on potential philanthropic supporters of Texas State University. Key tasks include prospect identification and research, basic portfolio management tasks, and fundraising strategy recommendations.</div><div>The Associate will specialize in individual prospect research, with a specific focus on wealth research. Additionally, the Associate will assist the frontline fundraisers in maintaining their portfolios of assigned prospects and assist in maintaining the prospect pipeline. Additional duties include maintaining constituent records, leading specific research projects, recommending best practices, and assisting in recognizing and identifying the need for process improvements</div> Development <ul><li>Proven ability to collaborate closely within a team while managing independent projects.</li><li>High level of computer literacy with experience in online research.</li><li>Experience with data entry, data analysis, databases, or working with data sets.</li><li>Experience in training, teaching, advising, or similar service-oriented role; the ability to listen, interpret, and process information and respond with suggestions based on the needs of the end-user.</li><li>Strong analytical, writing, and presentation skills with the ability to synthesize, organize, material from multiple sources.</li><li>Experience presenting and articulating findings clearly and concisely both verbally and in writing.</li><li>Highly organized and able to track and manage multiple projects simultaneously, prioritize work projects, and meet deadlines with minimal supervision.</li><li>Demonstrated proficiency and experience using Microsoft Excel, Word, Outlook and experience with other components of Microsoft Office suite to organize, format, and present data.</li></ul> <ul><li>Bachelor’s degree.</li><li>Proficiency in online tools for foundation, corporate, and individual research.</li><li>Previous experience in wealth research or asset valuation.</li><li>Previous work experience in a fundraising support role.</li><li>Proficiency in LexisNexis, ResearchPoint, Tableau, Banner, Foundation Directory Online, NOZA, Raiser’s Edge Fundraising Software, Microsoft Power BI, SPSS, SQL or similar databases.</li><li>Demonstrated advanced skills in Microsoft Excel and Microsoft Word with experience using pivot tables, charts and graphs, word merges, and design templates.</li><li>Ability to work from a solution driven prospective; able to recognize problems and develop detailed solutions with a plan for implementation.</li><li>Adept at working both independently as well as collaboratively.</li><li>Previous experience recommending process improvements and technology tools.</li></ul> <div>Are you passionate about higher education accessibility? Do you enjoy detail-oriented work and being a part of a collaborative team? If so, the Prospect Development Associate role may just be the perfect opportunity for you to join the team at Texas State University.</div><div>The Prospect Development Associate position plays a vital role in sustaining the mission of the University Advancement division. The Associate is responsible for identifying and gathering intel on potential philanthropic supporters of Texas State University. Key tasks include prospect identification and research, basic portfolio management tasks, and fundraising strategy recommendations.</div><div>The Associate will specialize in individual prospect research, with a specific focus on wealth research. Additionally, the Associate will assist the frontline fundraisers in maintaining their portfolios of assigned prospects and assist in maintaining the prospect pipeline. Additional duties include maintaining constituent records, leading specific research projects, recommending best practices, and assisting in recognizing and identifying the need for process improvements</div> <ul><li>Identifying, evaluating, and recommending potential philanthropic supporters of Texas State University and providing input on fundraising strategy.</li><li>Lead proactive wealth screenings for the team.</li><li>Provide research and analysis of biographical, philanthropic, professional, and financial/asset data in the form of written bios, summaries, event bios, and prospect lists.</li><li>Tracking prospects and donors through monitoring daily news, online alerts, and utilizing internal information. Identifying acquaintances through relationship mapping to facilitate institutional involvement.</li><li>Leading specific prospect research projects with supervisor guidance.</li><li>Supervising and delegating work duties to student workers as needed.</li><li>Assist with maintaining the donor database and keeping records updated through data entry, data audits, and other database related tasks as needed.</li><li>Meet with development staff to support activities, initiatives, and portfolios; assist in developing recommendations and strategies to help the fundraising team meet goals.</li><li>Assist in the identification and selection of new research resources; assist in the evaluation and selection of vendor services.</li><li>Assist in analyzing best practices for donor giving and identifying opportunities to improve business practices.</li><li>Maintain and uphold the professional and ethical standards set by the Association of Professional Researchers for Advancement (APRA).</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57762 2026-07-10T10:06:56-05:00 2026-07-10T10:06:57-05:00 Administrative Assistant II <div>The Administrative Assistant II provides administrative and general clerical support to the Bachelor’s in Public Administration and the Master’s in Public Administration programs and secondarily to the department of Political Science as a whole.</div> Political Science <ul><li>Ability to provide clear, concise written and verbal information.</li><li>Ability to establish rapport with internal and external constituents.</li><li>Ability to understand and interpret general university, college, department, and program policies and procedures.</li><li>Working knowledge of Microsoft Office programs, including Word, Excel, and Access.</li><li>Ability to organize and prioritize work.</li><li>Ability to independently resolve problems.</li><li>Ability to develop and maintain accurate and comprehensive records and files.</li></ul> <ul><li>Bachelor’s or Master’s Degree.</li><li>Previous experience in higher education.</li><li>Previous experience preparing purchases orders and compliance forms.</li><li>Knowledge of centralized automated accounting systems.</li><li>Experience with Texas State programs, including SAP, LOGI, SLATE, Concur, and Banner.</li></ul> <div>The Administrative Assistant II provides administrative and general clerical support to the Bachelor’s in Public Administration and the Master’s in Public Administration programs and secondarily to the department of Political Science as a whole.</div> <ul><li>Answer telephones, screen and transfer calls, take messages, and refer to other offices as appropriate all inquiries about the online BPA program.</li><li>Assist in managing the academic operations of the BPA and MPA programs.</li><li>Compose program correspondence, files, and forms that track program and student progress.</li><li>Coordinate meetings, maintain compliance forms, and prepare various events and activities.</li><li>Organize and prioritize work.</li><li>Maintain program director calendar.</li><li>Coordinate arrangements for meetings.</li><li>Prepare and review purchase orders and invoices.</li><li>Maintain ledgers.</li><li>Monitor due dates of all assignments and projects.</li><li>Supervise student workers.</li><li>Prepare Travel documents.</li><li>Assist in tasks supporting the department and other tasks as assigned.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57705 2026-07-03T10:01:58-05:00 2026-07-03T10:01:59-05:00 Research IT Specialist <div>The Research IT Specialist provides operational and technical support for the Division of Research technology environment, including desktop systems, enterprise applications, electronic research administration (eRA) platforms, websites, conferencing technologies, and emerging AI-enabled tools.<br><br></div><div>This position serves as a primary resource for troubleshooting hardware, software, authentication, networking, and systems access issues while supporting secure, reliable, and efficient technology operations. The Specialist assists with administration of research administration systems, website maintenance, workflow automation tools, analytics resources, and user support services.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate is a customer-focused technology professional with strong troubleshooting skills, the ability to manage multiple priorities, and the ability to communicate technical information to diverse audiences.</div> Research IT <ul><li>Bachelor's degree and three years of related experience.</li><li>Experience supporting hardware, operating systems, enterprise applications, endpoint technologies, networking, and user devices in a multi-user environment.</li><li>Experience troubleshooting software, authentication, access, application performance, and systems integration issues.</li><li>Experience supporting websites, web applications, content management systems, or web-based platforms.</li><li>Strong and responsive customer service, communication, training, documentation, organizational, and problem-solving skills.</li><li>Ability to maintain confidentiality and safeguard sensitive institutional and research information.&nbsp;</li></ul> <ul><li>Experience supporting eRA systems such as Kuali, Cayuse, Huron, InfoEd, Streamlyne, or similar platforms.</li><li>Experience supporting AI tools, workflow automation solutions, analytics platforms, dashboards, or reporting systems.</li><li>Experience with website platforms such as WordPress, SharePoint, Drupal, Gato, Calico, or similar technologies.</li><li>Experience with endpoint management, software deployment, cybersecurity practices, vulnerability remediation, or IT asset management.</li><li>Familiarity with research administration, sponsored programs, compliance operations, or higher education environments.</li></ul> <div>The Research IT Specialist provides operational and technical support for the Division of Research technology environment, including desktop systems, enterprise applications, electronic research administration (eRA) platforms, websites, conferencing technologies, and emerging AI-enabled tools.<br><br></div><div>This position serves as a primary resource for troubleshooting hardware, software, authentication, networking, and systems access issues while supporting secure, reliable, and efficient technology operations. The Specialist assists with administration of research administration systems, website maintenance, workflow automation tools, analytics resources, and user support services.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate is a customer-focused technology professional with strong troubleshooting skills, the ability to manage multiple priorities, and the ability to communicate technical information to diverse audiences.</div> <ul><li>Provide technical support for desktop hardware, laptops, mobile devices, printers, operating systems, peripherals, and enterprise applications.</li><li>Troubleshoot and resolve hardware, software, networking, authentication, access, and systems integration issues.</li><li>Support administration and user assistance for eRA systems and related proposal, compliance, and award management platforms.</li><li>Maintain user accounts, permissions, role-based security, and access controls for departmental and enterprise systems.</li><li>Support departmental websites, web applications, content management systems, and web-based services.</li><li>Assist with implementation and support of workflow automation, reporting tools, dashboards, AI-enabled solutions, and operational technologies.</li><li>Support conferencing, audiovisual, livestreaming, and hybrid meeting technologies for research operations and events.</li><li>Coordinate with university IT, vendors, developers, and functional offices to resolve issues and implement technology improvements.</li><li>Create and maintain technical documentation, training materials, knowledge-base resources, inventory records, and standard operating procedures.</li><li>Monitor technology resources for performance, security, reliability, and compliance and perform other duties as assigned.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57700 2026-07-03T07:42:09-05:00 2026-07-03T07:42:10-05:00 Industry and Internship Coordinator <div>The Industry Relations and Internship Coordinator supports the Construction Science and Management (CSM) and Concrete Industry Management (CIM) programs at Texas State University by serving as a central liaison between the programs, students, and industry partners. This position cultivates strong relationships with construction and concrete industry stakeholders, coordinates student internship placement, and organizes events to enhance student engagement and industry visibility. Under the supervision of the Department Chair, this role ensures that program-industry partnerships remain robust, students are well-prepared for the workforce, and program activities align with college and university priorities.</div> Department of Engineering Technology <div>• Bachelor’s Degree in a field related to construction, engineering, business, education, or project management.<br>• Minimum 5 years of relevant experience in an administrative, industry<br>relations, workforce development, or management role.<br>• Demonstrated experience developing and sustaining strategic partnerships with external stakeholders.<br>• Proven professionalism and experience working with internal and external<br>audiences, including industry partners, volunteers, students, faculty, and<br>alumni.</div> <div>• Master’s degree in a field related to construction, engineering, business, education, or project management.&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple priorities<br>simultaneously.<br>• Self-directed and motivated with a collaborative mindset, committed to<br>continuous improvement.<br>• Proficiency with Microsoft Office and willingness to learn university data<br>systems and relationship management platforms.<br>• Strong written and verbal communication skills; proven success in building<br>connections and relationships.<br>• Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment.<br>• Experience supervising and mentoring students.<br>• Ability to plan, implement, and evaluate initiatives, with critical thinking and decision-making skills.<br>• Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a dynamic environment.</div> <div>The Industry Relations and Internship Coordinator supports the Construction Science and Management (CSM) and Concrete Industry Management (CIM) programs at Texas State University by serving as a central liaison between the programs, students, and industry partners. This position cultivates strong relationships with construction and concrete industry stakeholders, coordinates student internship placement, and organizes events to enhance student engagement and industry visibility. Under the supervision of the Department Chair, this role ensures that program-industry partnerships remain robust, students are well-prepared for the workforce, and program activities align with college and university priorities.</div> <div>40% Industry Relations<br>• Cultivate, strengthen, and expand collaborative relationships with industry<br>partners in construction, concrete, and related fields.<br>• Coordinate industry visits, site tours, guest speakers, and classroom<br>engagement opportunities.<br>• Assist industry recruiters in connecting with students for internships,<br>employment, and career fairs.<br>• Support departmental industry advisory councils, including identifying<br>potential members, preparing meeting agendas, coordinating<br>communications, and producing reports.<br>• Represent the CSM and CIM programs at regional and national conferences,<br>competitions, and industry events.<br>• Develop industry-focused reports and maintain an active database of partners<br>and contacts.<br>30% Internship Coordination<br>• Serve as the primary coordinator for CSM and CIM student internships.<br>• Develop and maintain relationships with companies offering internships;<br>expand opportunities across Texas and beyond.<br>• Match students with appropriate internship experiences and provide pre-<br>Texas State University HR Site :: Posting Print Preview https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/hr/postings/57061/print_preview<br>1 of 6 6/18/2026, 10:16 AM<br>placement advising.<br>• Track, evaluate, and report internship participation and outcomes.<br>• Collaborate with faculty to integrate internship experiences into academic<br>requirements and ensure compliance with accreditation standards.<br>• Maintain communication with employers to ensure student performance<br>meets industry expectations.<br>10% Event Planning &amp; Student Engagement<br>• Plan and execute program events such as Career Fairs, corporate lunch and<br>learns and mixers, scholarship galas, advisory board meetings, industry<br>information sessions, graduating student banquets, and other student/industry<br>focused events.<br>• Support student organizations affiliated with the programs, including CSA,<br>AGC, CAWIC and ACI student chapters, by advising on event planning and<br>professional development activities.<br>• Collaborate with Career Services on successful execution of career fairs.<br>• Coordinate logistics for competitions, conferences, and networking activities<br>that connect students with industry professionals.<br>• Oversee promotional and marketing activities to highlight program<br>achievements and industry partnerships.<br>10% Recruiting<br>• Actively recruit new students to the CSM and CIM programs through outreach<br>to high schools, community colleges, and industry partners.<br>• Coordinate with the CIM Program Marketing and Recruiting Coordinator for<br>the effective use of promotional materials in support of recruiting efforts.<br>• Represent the programs at career fairs, recruiting events, and professional<br>conferences.<br>• Develop recruitment materials and presentations in collaboration with the<br>department and university marketing teams.<br>• Engage current students, alumni, and industry partners in recruitment<br>initiatives.<br>• Track and analyze recruitment efforts to support program growth and<br>continuous improvement.<br>10% Other Duties as Assigned<br>• Assist with program-level accreditation and reporting (ABET, ACCE, and other<br>relevant bodies).<br>• Contribute to departmental communications, website updates, and marketing<br>materials.<br>• Support fundraising and advancement initiatives in collaboration with the<br>department and external foundations.<br>• Supervise and mentor student assistants supporting program activities.<br>• Provide input on curriculum support related to marketable skills, resume<br>development, and interview preparation.</div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57692 2026-07-02T13:03:56-05:00 2026-07-02T13:03:57-05:00 Assistant Director, Facilities & Grounds <div>The Assistant Director of Facilities and Grounds will lead and manage the administration and operation of the Facilities program, consisting of all Campus Recreation special events, Grounds Operations, Custodial Operations and Building Maintenance Operations in the pursuit of inspiring Bobcats to be their best and create lasting memories. The Assistant Director will also be responsible for the development and oversight of an 8-person Custodial team, two Maintenance Worker II positions, and a 5-person Grounds crew.</div> Campus Recreation <ul><li>Minimum of two years of professional work experience within facility operations (e.g. Campus Recreation, Fitness, Aquatics, Outdoors, etc.) or related field</li><li>Bachelor’s degree in Recreation, Exercise Science, Health Education, Sport Management, Turf Management, Higher Education, or related field</li><li>Progressively responsible experience within campus recreation or related field.</li><li>Current CPR, AED, First Aid and or ability to obtain within 45 days</li></ul> <ul><li>Experience supervising full time staff in a higher education setting</li><li>Master’s degree in Recreation, Exercise Science, Health Education, Sport Management, Turf Management, Higher Education, or related field</li><li>In-depth knowledge of turfgrass species, cultivation practices, soil science, irrigation systems, pest management, and turf equipment operation</li><li>Current Texas Department of Agriculture Pesticide Applicator License</li></ul> <div>The Assistant Director of Facilities and Grounds will lead and manage the administration and operation of the Facilities program, consisting of all Campus Recreation special events, Grounds Operations, Custodial Operations and Building Maintenance Operations in the pursuit of inspiring Bobcats to be their best and create lasting memories. The Assistant Director will also be responsible for the development and oversight of an 8-person Custodial team, two Maintenance Worker II positions, and a 5-person Grounds crew.</div> <div><strong>Facility Management/Maintenance, Turf Maintenance: 30%</strong></div><ul><li>Develop and manage a diverse Facilities program including the administration of all campus recreation grounds operations, custodial operations and building maintenance operations.</li><li>Oversee the daily facility activities, including custodial, maintenance, repairs and safety inspections on facility systems, including HVAC, plumbing, electrical and structural components. Oversee the preparation and upkeep of sports fields, including mowing, fertilization and pest control to ensure optimal playing conditions.</li><li>Oversee work order and asset management tracking systems.</li><li>Implement innovative ideas that align with strategic plan and department priorities to improve overall operations and growth of programs/services/usage.</li><li>Develop and conduct assessments of program goals annually. Report assessment results to leadership as documentation of programmatic outcomes supporting department and division goals.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Staff Development and Oversight: 30%</strong></div><ul><li>Oversee the development and performance evaluation of an 8-person Custodial team, two Maintenance Worker II positions, and a 5-person Grounds crew.</li><li>Meet with full time staff regularly to discuss program goals, professional goals and area updates.</li><li>Develop and oversee staff schedules and project lists to ensure timely completion and tracking.</li><li>With the potential to hire, train, supervise, and evaluate approximately 5 student staff.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Administration and Budget Development: 20%</strong></div><ul><li>Lead annual budget development process in collaboration with Coordinator, Maintenance Worker II and Grounds crew.</li><li>Plan, prepare and manage program budgets including overseeing income projections and monitoring income, expenses, and yearly comparisons.</li><li>Purchase equipment and supplies.</li><li>Approve staff time and ensure compliance with payroll and purchasing processes.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Risk Management and Safety: 10%</strong></div><ul><li>Ensure staff compliance with industry standard safety and risk management practices, facility and equipment inspections, and established Campus Recreation policies and procedures.</li><li>Knowledge of applicable regulations, environmental guidelines, and safety standards governing turf management practices. Familiarity with pesticide regulations, water conservation measures, and environmental sustainability initiatives.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Other Duties: 10%</strong></div><ul><li>Actively participate in departmental programs and projects designed to support the mission and goals of the university, division, and department.</li><li>Serve on committees and task forces, as assigned.</li><li>Other duties as requested or required, whether or not specifically mentioned in this job description.</li><li>This position requires a flexible work schedule which at times will require frequent attendance during evenings and weekends. Additional hours may be required during peak periods.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57683 2026-07-02T08:36:51-05:00 2026-07-02T08:36:52-05:00 Disability Specialist <div>The Disability Specialist position works with students with disabilities to facilitate<br>access to the educational environment. The Disability Specialist is responsible for<br>collaborating with faculty and staff to improve accessibility and promote an inclusive<br>environment. This position assists in the coordination of activities which increase<br>disability awareness within the Texas State University community.</div> Disability Services <ul><li>Bachelor’s degree in Education, Psychology, Social Work, or a related field, or a combination of education and experience that demonstrates the necessary knowledge, skills, and abilities.</li><li>Experience working in a disability related academic or clinical setting.</li><li>Ability to work independently with minimal supervision, as well as collaboratively as an effective team member.</li><li>Excellent interpersonal skills, encompassing both oral and written communication abilities.</li></ul> <ul><li>Master’s degree in Education, Psychology, Social Work, Counseling, or related field.</li><li>Strong ability to understand and address the unique needs of college students with disabilities, with a genuine interest in providing one-on-one support to meet their accessibility requirements in an academic environment.</li><li>Proficiency in interpreting a range of educational, psychological, and medical documentation.</li><li>Knowledge of disability law, including the Americans with Disabilities Act and Section 504, and its practical application for students with disabilities.</li><li>Knowledge of the Accessible Information Management (AIM) database.</li></ul> <div>The Disability Specialist position works with students with disabilities to facilitate<br>access to the educational environment. The Disability Specialist is responsible for<br>collaborating with faculty and staff to improve accessibility and promote an inclusive<br>environment. This position assists in the coordination of activities which increase<br>disability awareness within the Texas State University community.</div> <ul><li>Provides ongoing service and case management to students with disabilities, including monitoring the effectiveness of accommodations, offering individual advocacy, and making referrals to relevant campus services and programs.</li><li>Offers resources that cater to the unique needs of students with disabilities, focusing on strategies specific to Texas State University.</li><li>Conducts meetings with students who request accommodations, which involves gathering, interpreting, and validating documentation (e.g., student self-reports, medical records, school records) provided by the student. Through an interactive process, assesses the student’s disability and its impact on academic performance and campus engagement to determine appropriate accommodations.</li><li>Provides consultation and training to faculty and staff on accessibility issues and laws, serving as a knowledgeable resource for the accessibility needs and rights of students with disabilities.</li><li>Participates in disability outreach and awareness events.</li><li>Assists in the development and/or review of office publications, policies, and procedures.</li><li>Represents the department in university, division, and departmental committees and task forces.</li><li>Stays updated on research and best practices concerning students with disabilities in higher education.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57631 2026-07-01T10:33:41-05:00 2026-07-01T10:33:42-05:00 Assistant Director, Direct Response <div>The Assistant Director for Direct Response is responsible for planning, implementing, and optimizing direct response fundraising campaigns that generate philanthropic support for Texas State University.<br><br>The Assistant Director supports strategic fundraising communications and donor initiatives that strengthen philanthropic participation across Texas State University. This position develops and executes multi-channel fundraising campaigns designed to acquire, retain, and upgrade donors while supporting pipeline development.<br><br></div><div>This role analyzes engagement and campaign performance data to identify opportunities for growth and translate insights into actionable fundraising strategies. The Assistant Director collaborates closely with Donor Engagement, Alumni Engagement, and Major Gifts to align communications with fundraising priorities and strengthen the donor journey from participation to deeper philanthropic investment.<br><br></div> Development <ul><li>Bachelor’s degree in communications, marketing, journalism, public relations, nonprofit management, or related field.</li><li>Three years of professional experience in fundraising communications, annual giving, direct response marketing, advancement communications, or related field.</li><li>Demonstrated experience analyzing communication, fundraising, or engagement data and applying insights to improve campaign performance.</li><li>Experience developing donor-facing fundraising communications and campaign messaging.</li><li>Strong project management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines simultaneously.</li><li>Strong interpersonal and collaborative skills with the ability to work effectively across teams and stakeholders.</li></ul> <ul><li>Experience working in higher education advancement, nonprofit fundraising, or donor communications.</li><li>Experience supporting annual giving, leadership annual giving, crowdfunding, or direct response fundraising initiatives.</li><li>Experience utilizing audience segmentation strategies and donor engagement data.</li><li>Familiarity with CRM, email marketing, and fundraising platforms such as Blackbaud, Luminate, Salesforce, GiveCampus, or similar systems.</li><li>Experience supporting integrated multi-channel fundraising campaigns.</li><li>Experience leveraging approved generative AI tools to draft, edit, summarize, or enhance communications while exercising professional judgment and adhering to university privacy and data security policies.</li></ul> <div>The Assistant Director for Direct Response is responsible for planning, implementing, and optimizing direct response fundraising campaigns that generate philanthropic support for Texas State University.<br><br>The Assistant Director supports strategic fundraising communications and donor initiatives that strengthen philanthropic participation across Texas State University. This position develops and executes multi-channel fundraising campaigns designed to acquire, retain, and upgrade donors while supporting pipeline development.<br><br></div><div>This role analyzes engagement and campaign performance data to identify opportunities for growth and translate insights into actionable fundraising strategies. The Assistant Director collaborates closely with Donor Engagement, Alumni Engagement, and Major Gifts to align communications with fundraising priorities and strengthen the donor journey from participation to deeper philanthropic investment.<br><br></div> <ul><li>Analyze donor engagement metrics, fundraising campaign performance, and communication effectiveness to identify opportunities for growth and optimization.</li><li>Translate campaign and engagement data into actionable recommendations supporting donor acquisition, retention, reactivation, and upgrade strategies.</li><li>Develop and execute direct response fundraising communications in partnership with Advancement Marketing across email, social media, web, print, and emerging channels.</li><li>Lead communications strategies supporting giving days, crowdfunding efforts, and targeted fundraising initiatives.</li><li>Develop audience segmentation strategies and donor journeys that strengthen participation and philanthropic engagement.</li><li>Collaborate with Donor Engagement, Alumni Engagement, and Major Gifts teams to align messaging with fundraising priorities and donor engagement goals.</li><li>Support planning, development, and execution of integrated fundraising campaigns across multiple channels.</li><li>Conduct message testing and evaluate audience performance to improve fundraising outcomes and communication effectiveness.</li><li>Review fundraising communications to ensure consistency in messaging, tone, accuracy, and alignment with advancement priorities.</li><li>Assist with communications planning supporting giving days, annual campaigns, and other fundraising priorities.</li><li>Build collaborative relationships across campus to support fundraising communications efforts and identify opportunities for donor engagement.</li><li>Able to travel and willing to work occasional evening and weekend hours as required for events and advancement initiatives.</li><li>Other duties as assigned.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57618 2026-06-30T16:24:28-05:00 2026-06-30T16:24:29-05:00 Plant Mechanic I <div>Responsible for the maintenance of all equipment associated with the production of steam, chilled water, and electricity.</div> Facilities Services <ul><li>Understanding of basic mechanical concepts of rotating equipment, chillers, boilers, and generators for proper functioning and repair.</li><li>Familiarity with chemical safety practices and Safety Data Sheets (SDS).</li><li>Knowledge of standard safety practices, including the use of respiratory equipment.</li><li>Ability to work effectively as a team member and interact courteously with others.</li><li>Experience using large hand tools, pipe fitting, seals, filters, and lubricants.</li><li>Ability to complete computer-based time sheets, record data, read and write work orders, follow standard operating procedures, and use specialized measuring devices.</li></ul><div><br></div> <ul><li>Possess an EPA Section 608 Universal Technician Certification.</li><li>Experience working in a higher education environment.</li><li>Proficiency in using AiM Integrated Work Management System.</li></ul><div><br></div> <div>Responsible for the maintenance of all equipment associated with the production of steam, chilled water, and electricity.</div> <ul><li>Conduct mechanical equipment, piping and valve preventive maintenance tasks and document.</li><li>Inspect multiple 550-ton to 2,500-ton chillers.</li><li>Maintain plant air compressor and dryers for instrument air in plant.</li><li>Inspect and lubricate large vertical, horizontal, and centrifugal split case pumps and motors.</li><li>Inspect, clean cooling tower fans, gearboxes, piping, valves, and basins in cooling towers.</li><li>Complete and close out work orders.</li><li>Inspect and service multiple boilers up to 50,000 pounds per hour steam.</li><li>Assist and service emergency generators on campus as needed.</li><li>Inspect and maintain sand filters, reverse osmosis units, and water softeners.</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned.</li></ul><div><br></div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57559 2026-06-29T09:07:16-05:00 2026-06-29T09:07:17-05:00 Sr Psychologist <div>Texas State University Counseling Center strives to provide services and programs within a framework of professional competence, affirmation, and responsiveness to a variety of lived experiences. The staff seeks professional colleagues interested in joining a collaborative and positive team that is committed to providing services to support all students in our culturally and economically varied campus community. Located within the Division of Student Success and accredited by IACS, the Center is also proud to host a well-respected APA-accredited doctoral internship program as well as practicum training and a post-doctoral residency.<br><br></div><div>In addition to general professional staff duties, this position provides coordination and leadership for the Center’s Anxiety and Stress Management Initiative. The position works with the Associate Director/Clinical Services, the Director, and other Center Leadership to refine the vision, mission, operations, and staffing of the Anxiety Initiative. This position will collaboratively structure the elements of the Initiative with attention to the phase in period; refine program development, delivery and assessment; collaborate with other areas within the Center to share staffing and program resources to serve the needs of student participants; and provide services within a high demand/fast paced setting.<br><br></div><div>Successful candidates will have a generalist orientation and evidence knowledge and experiences responsive to the needs of a vibrant university community. Further, they will possess specific interests and experiences in providing developmentally-based services which support the mission of an engaged university counseling center.<br><br></div> Counseling Center <ul><li>Licensure as a psychologist in Texas (or other location eligible for Texas psychology licensure at the doctoral level). Texas license must be obtained within 12 months of start date and must be maintained to remain eligible for employment.</li><li>4-6 years <strong>post psychologist licensure</strong> experience in managing or providing services for anxiety or mood management</li><li>Experience in providing manualized and/or time effective services for anxiety concerns</li><li>Experience in managing a clinical intervention program or project</li><li>Eligibility to provide clinical supervision in an APA accredited training program</li><li>Experience in providing crisis intervention services</li><li>Experience in developing and providing prevention related programming for a college-aged population</li><li>Strong interpersonal, oral and written communication skills</li></ul> <ul><li>A minimum of two years of clinical experience in a higher education counseling setting or with a similar adult population (may include doctoral internship, postdoctoral residency or practicum experiences).</li><li>1-2 years engaging with a program or initiative focused on reducing clinical concerns/enhancing resiliency</li><li>Additional interests and experience in one or more of the following areas is highly preferred: assessment/ data management, center operations, crisis management, mindfulness, groups, clinical training/supervision, skills-based interventions, or substance use/abuse.</li><li>Experience actively engaging in practice with populations evidencing a variety of life experiences.</li><li>Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with colleagues, campus departments, and student groups</li><li>Experience working as a member of a clinically based professional team (including related academic training).</li><li>Experience within a multifaceted framework involving strongly linked clinical and training efforts.</li></ul> <div>Texas State University Counseling Center strives to provide services and programs within a framework of professional competence, affirmation, and responsiveness to a variety of lived experiences. The staff seeks professional colleagues interested in joining a collaborative and positive team that is committed to providing services to support all students in our culturally and economically varied campus community. Located within the Division of Student Success and accredited by IACS, the Center is also proud to host a well-respected APA-accredited doctoral internship program as well as practicum training and a post-doctoral residency.<br><br></div><div>In addition to general professional staff duties, this position provides coordination and leadership for the Center’s Anxiety and Stress Management Initiative. The position works with the Associate Director/Clinical Services, the Director, and other Center Leadership to refine the vision, mission, operations, and staffing of the Anxiety Initiative. This position will collaboratively structure the elements of the Initiative with attention to the phase in period; refine program development, delivery and assessment; collaborate with other areas within the Center to share staffing and program resources to serve the needs of student participants; and provide services within a high demand/fast paced setting.<br><br></div><div>Successful candidates will have a generalist orientation and evidence knowledge and experiences responsive to the needs of a vibrant university community. Further, they will possess specific interests and experiences in providing developmentally-based services which support the mission of an engaged university counseling center.<br><br></div> <ul><li>Responsibilities include:</li><li>Daily management of the Anxiety Initiative</li><li>Develop/refine group and individual training opportunities</li><li>Marketing and services promotion</li><li>Recruit, select, and supervise graduate staff, as available</li><li>Engagement and training with appropriate Center and campus constituents important to developing the Anxiety Initiative including academic and Student Success partners.</li><li>Time-effective personal counseling (individual, group, and limited relationship services), initial assessments &amp; triage, crisis intervention, clinical training &amp; supervision, outreach programming, campus training, consultation, assessment, and administrative duties, as assigned.</li><li>In addition to the general duties noted above, interest and experience in one or more of the following areas is highly preferred; data management, groups, services to students possessing varied lived experiences, mind body principles, clinical training/supervision, crisis management, skills-based interventions, or substance use/abuse.</li><li>Competitive candidates will possess strong interpersonal, oral and written communication skills; a demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with colleagues, campus departments, and student groups; a commitment to actively engage in practice with populations experiencing a variety of lived experiences; value a multifaceted approach involving strongly linked clinical and training efforts; possess interpersonal flexibility; ability/experience providing services within a high demand/fast paced setting; exhibit an awareness of the importance of life balance; and a commitment to the importance of the developmental aspect of university counseling services.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57291 2026-06-04T07:47:34-05:00 2026-06-04T07:47:34-05:00 Police Officer <div>Texas State University (TXST) Police Department is looking for lateral transfers who are motivated to help others and be a part of the UPD Team. Every day our officers work with students, faculty, staff and the community to ensure safety for everyone. Here at TXST we are committed to having a workforce that resembles the people of Texas and the University we serve.</div> UPD Operations <ul><li>High School Diploma or equivalent.</li><li>Be licensed by TCOLE; or be a certified or licensed out of state peace officer and successfully obtain TCOLE licensing (basic peace officer or higher) within 90 days of hire.</li><li>Must have at least 1-year prior work experience as a full-time commissioned peace officer with similar duties in a comparable law enforcement agency.</li><li>Left previous agency with an honorable discharge.</li></ul> <ul><li>60 College Credit Hours / Associate’s Degree.</li><li>Bachelor’s Degree.</li><li>Previous work experience in university policing.</li><li>TCOLE Proficiency Certificate above Basic Peace Officer.</li><li>Current Full Time Working Peace Officer.</li></ul> <div>Texas State University (TXST) Police Department is looking for lateral transfers who are motivated to help others and be a part of the UPD Team. Every day our officers work with students, faculty, staff and the community to ensure safety for everyone. Here at TXST we are committed to having a workforce that resembles the people of Texas and the University we serve.</div> <ul><li>Enforcement of all laws of the State of Texas to include laws and ordinances for TXST University and the city of San Marcos.</li><li>Respond to emergency calls, traffic accidents and general requests for assistance.</li><li>Patrols university property to include campuses and leased properties.</li><li>Issues warnings and citations to violators of university, city and state regulations.</li><li>Conduct preliminary investigations into minor traffic crashes and crimes.</li><li>Writes offense, incident, arrest and impoundment reports in a timely manner.</li><li>Proper use of communication and recording equipment.</li><li>Appears in court and testifies under oath.</li><li>Performs special assignments as required, such as university events, investigations and parking enforcement or crime prevention.</li><li>Work 12-hour shifts, including nights, weekends and holidays.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57197 2026-05-28T08:26:15-05:00 2026-05-28T08:26:15-05:00 Grant Director- McNair Scholars <ul><li>This is a grant funded position. Continuation of this position is contingent upon grant funding.</li><li>The Director is responsible for the daily operation and facilitation of the programmatic and administrative components of the McNair Scholars program.</li><li>The Director will be responsible for coordinating and providing administrative oversight for all phases of the Program.</li><li>Primary duties involve implementation of program activities and services to meet specific program objectives.</li><li>Main office location at the Texas State University Campus in San Marcos, Texas.</li><li>Evening and weekend work may be required.</li></ul> McNair Scholars <ul><li>Doctoral degree in higher education administration, student development, counseling, social work, or STEM-related field.</li><li>Experience in collegiate teaching, administration, scholarly activities, developing research materials, or working with academic support programs to promote graduate school enrollment and doctoral degree attainment.</li><li>Knowledge of higher education academic programs, research, and scholarly activities.</li><li>Experience with academic support programs, or other student support services;</li><li>Experience advising students on academics, financial aid, college and career preparation.</li><li>Experience planning, coordinating, and implementing services for college students.</li><li>Experience managing programs, budgets, staff, and processes.</li></ul> <ul><li>Knowledge of TRIO or other higher education academic programs and support services and effective practices supporting student recruitment, retention, and development.</li><li>Three (3) years of experience in staff supervision, budget management, program development and evaluation, reporting, and compliance with federal regulations.</li><li>Five (5) years of experience in collegiate teaching, administration, scholarly activities, developing research materials, or working with academic support programs to promote graduate school enrollment and doctoral degree attainment.&nbsp;</li><li>2 years program management experience including fiscal management, database management, and staff supervision.</li><li>Bilingual (Spanish) speaking/writing.&nbsp;</li><li>Experience working with SAP/Excel for budgets and financial processes.</li></ul> <ul><li>This is a grant funded position. Continuation of this position is contingent upon grant funding.</li><li>The Director is responsible for the daily operation and facilitation of the programmatic and administrative components of the McNair Scholars program.</li><li>The Director will be responsible for coordinating and providing administrative oversight for all phases of the Program.</li><li>Primary duties involve implementation of program activities and services to meet specific program objectives.</li><li>Main office location at the Texas State University Campus in San Marcos, Texas.</li><li>Evening and weekend work may be required.</li></ul> <ul><li>Responsible for the daily operation of the program and all components associated with the program.</li><li>Conduct regularly scheduled group and individual meetings with program staff.</li><li>Prepare and administer program budget in accordance with federal and university budgetary policies and procedures.</li><li>Develop and implement strategies to meet program objectives.</li><li>Maintain relevant data and metrics on performance to measure and evaluate goals and objectives.</li><li>Develop and maintain processes for keeping accurate records. Monitor file/record keeping schedule in accordance with university guidelines. Conduct regularly schedule reviews of participant files and financial information.</li><li>Communicate and correspond with Department of Education Program officers on program performance (annual report), annual budgets, program needs, requests, progress updates and questions.</li><li>Work with university departments to resolve any issues that may arise as they pertain to budgets, financial analysis, reconciliations, procurement, travel, the hiring process, office maintenance or otherwise.</li><li>Attend State, Regional and National Conferences.</li><li>Other duties as assigned.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/56814 2026-04-17T12:55:15-05:00 2026-04-17T12:55:17-05:00 Lieutenant <div>Assist the Chief of Police with the administration, management and oversight of the University Police Department including rendering basic police services in an effort to reduce incidences of crime and enforce federal, state and local laws and ordinances.</div> UPD Operations <ul><li>Demonstrates effective supervisory and leadership skills in a law enforcement environment.</li><li>Communicates clearly and professionally, both verbally and in writing.</li><li>Uses computer applications proficiently to prepare reports, manage information, and support operational needs.</li><li>Interacts professionally and effectively with the public, in person, online, via email and by telephone.</li><li>Works independently and manages assignments and projects to timely completion.</li><li>Demonstrates working knowledge of law enforcement policies, procedures, and organizational operations.</li><li>Collaborates effectively with faculty, staff, students, and internal university departments to support departmental objectives.</li><li>Coordinates effectively with external organizations and law enforcement agencies.</li><li>Maintains flexibility to work varied schedules, including nights, weekends, and holidays, as operational needs require.</li><li>Possesses a minimum of two (2) years of experience as a police first‑line supervisor (Sergeant or equivalent).</li><li>Holds a TCOLE Intermediate or Advanced Peace Officer certification.</li></ul> <ul><li>Holds an Advanced TCOLE Peace Officer certification.</li><li>Demonstrates in‑depth knowledge of university policing operations and departmental general orders.</li><li>Bachelor’s degree in Criminal Justice, Public Administration, or a related field.</li><li>Master’s degree in Criminal Justice, Public Administration, or a related field.</li><li>Four (4) or more years of experience as a police first‑line supervisor.</li><li>Two (2) years of experience as a Sergeant within the Texas State University Police Department or Texas State University System.</li><li>Two (2) years of experience in a mid‑level police management role.</li><li>Completion of at least eighty (80) hours of recognized law enforcement leadership training (e.g., LEMIT, FBI‑LEEDA, FBI Academy).</li></ul> <div>Assist the Chief of Police with the administration, management and oversight of the University Police Department including rendering basic police services in an effort to reduce incidences of crime and enforce federal, state and local laws and ordinances.</div> <ul><li>Provides regular updates to the Operations Captain regarding critical operational issues, internal affairs matters, and criminal investigations.</li><li>Acts as a liaison with faculty, staff, students, and university leadership on departmental, administrative, and legislative matters affecting assigned areas.</li><li>Represents the Operations Captain and serves as a point of contact for civic and university community groups, when appropriate.</li><li>Participates in meetings with university personnel and external partners that may impact the command area.</li><li>Receives, reviews, and distributes correspondence related to assigned operational areas.</li><li>Responds to complaints and assigns or oversees internal affairs investigations, as required.</li><li>Oversees projects and initiatives delegated by the Operations Captain.</li><li>Coordinates and collaborates with other local, state, and federal law enforcement agencies.</li><li>Prepares, administers, and monitors budgets for designated functions or units.</li><li>Serves as Chairperson for the Awards Committee and Accident Review Committee.</li><li>Maintains documentation and archives related to critical incidents and newsworthy events.</li><li>Performs other duties as assigned by the Operations Captain.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/56534 2026-03-25T12:35:27-05:00 2026-03-25T12:35:29-05:00 Construction Manager I <div>Responsible for planning, designing, estimating, scheduling, directing, and inspecting small-sized renovation and construction projects to ensure objectives are met.</div> Facilities Planning Design <ul><li>Engineering and/or construction management education, training, and experience.</li><li>Intermediate-level mathematical as well as engineering skills are required.</li><li>Ability to confirm plan accuracy, develop take-off from plans, ability to reference estimations resources, process accurate projects cost and manage step-by-step construction, renovation, and maintenance projects is required.</li><li>Knowledge of drafting tools/techniques, ability to draft using CADD technology, application of standard architectural graphic standards and principles are required.</li><li>Reading ability: Understand, interpret, and apply complex legal and technical documents, contracts for construction, blueprints, and schematics.</li><li>Communicate and negotiate project requests to a variety of clients including staff, administrators, faculty, students, and contractors.</li><li>Writing skill: Prepare clear, concise, correct reports, letters, specifications, CADD drawings and estimates.</li><li>Successfully interact with and interpret requests from a wide variety of clients, direct the work of others, work as a team member/leader, and negotiate/mitigate personnel challenges.</li><li>Facilitation skills. Experience using personal computers.</li><li>Prepare business correspondence, policy/proposal development reports.</li></ul><div><br></div> <div>Bachelor’s degree in related field</div> <div>Responsible for planning, designing, estimating, scheduling, directing, and inspecting small-sized renovation and construction projects to ensure objectives are met.</div> <ul><li>Manage, monitor and direct contracts with contractors, architects, engineers, consultants for assigned projects.</li><li>Plan, design, schedule and estimate various requests for new construction projects, facility modification/renovation or major maintenance.</li><li>Evaluate and make recommendations on facility conditions, renovations, and repairs.</li><li>Develop specifications for goods and services by researching vendor data and referencing applicable codes, regulations and standards.</li><li>Prepare project contract documents including contract change orders and addendums.</li><li>Meet with project requestors, interpret requests for feasibility and prioritize projects.</li><li>Assist in developing various reports, plans, budgets and schedules.</li><li>Keep project files.</li><li>Other duties as assigned.</li></ul> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/56226 2026-03-02T09:17:59-06:00 2026-03-02T09:18:00-06:00 Temporary Positions - Craft Worker <div>What makes Texas State unique is the people who work here. Texas State University seeks candidates whose professional background includes embracing cooperation and ideas, a global perspective, and a commitment to community-building.&nbsp;</div> Human Resources <div>What makes Texas State unique is the people who work here. Texas State University seeks candidates whose professional background includes embracing cooperation and ideas, a global perspective, and a commitment to community-building.&nbsp;</div> <div>Occupations where workers perform jobs that require special manual skills and a comprehensive knowledge of the processes involved in the work which is required through on-the-job training and experience or apprenticeship or other formal training programs. Craftwork occupations include mechanics and repairers, electricians, heavy equipment operators, stationary engineers, skilled machining occupations, carpenters, compositors and typesetters, power plant operators, and kindred workers.<br><br>Texas State Craft Worker title examples: Locksmith; Electrician; Auto Mechanic&nbsp;</div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/56224 2026-03-02T09:14:52-06:00 2026-03-02T09:14:52-06:00 Temporary Positions - Laborer <div>What makes Texas State unique is the people who work here. Texas State University seeks candidates whose professional background includes embracing cooperation and ideas,, a global perspective, and a commitment to community-building. &nbsp;</div> Human Resources <div>What makes Texas State unique is the people who work here. Texas State University seeks candidates whose professional background includes embracing cooperation and ideas,, a global perspective, and a commitment to community-building. &nbsp;</div> <div>Occupations in which workers perform duties that result in or contribute to the comfort, convenience, hygiene, or safety of the general public or which contribute to the upkeep and care of buildings, facilities, or grounds of public property. Workers in this group may operate machinery. Includes: chauffeurs, laundry and dry cleaning operatives, truck drivers, bus drivers, garage laborers, custodial employees, gardeners, groundskeepers, refuse collectors, construction workers, park rangers(maintenance), farm workers (except managers), craft apprentices/trainees/helpers, and kindred workers.<br><br>Texas State Laborer title examples: Driver; Custodian; Grounds Maintenance Worker &nbsp;</div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/56222 2026-03-02T09:05:06-06:00 2026-03-02T09:05:06-06:00 Temporary Positions - Service Worker <div>What makes Texas State unique is the people who work here. Texas State University seeks candidates whose professional background includes embracing cooperation and ideas,, a global perspective, and a commitment to community-building. &nbsp;</div> Human Resources <div>What makes Texas State unique is the people who work here. Texas State University seeks candidates whose professional background includes embracing cooperation and ideas,, a global perspective, and a commitment to community-building. &nbsp;</div> <div>Occupations in which workers perform service-related duties for the general public. Workers in this group may operate machinery. Includes: hospitality, restaurant/food employees, hotel and lodgings services, and kindred workers.<br><br>Texas State Service Worker title examples: Cashier; Mail Clerk; Cook</div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/56220 2026-03-02T08:56:44-06:00 2026-03-02T08:56:44-06:00 Temporary Positions - Technician <div>What makes Texas State unique is the people who work here. Texas State University seeks candidates whose professional background includes embracing cooperation and ideas,, a global perspective, and a commitment to community-building.</div> Human Resources <div>What makes Texas State unique is the people who work here. Texas State University seeks candidates whose professional background includes embracing cooperation and ideas,, a global perspective, and a commitment to community-building.</div> <div>Occupations that require a combination of basic scientific or technical knowledge and manual skills which can be obtained through specialized post-secondary school education or equivalent on-the-job training. Technician occupations include computer programmers, drafters, surveyors, licensed practical nurses, photographers, radio operators, technical illustrators, highway technicians, technicians (medical, dental, electronic, physical sciences), police and fire sergeants, inspectors (production or processing inspectors, testers and weighers), kindred workers.<br><br>Texas State Technician title examples: Medical Technologist; Lab Services Tech; Child Care Teacher&nbsp;</div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/56218 2026-03-02T08:43:18-06:00 2026-03-02T08:43:19-06:00 Temporary Positions - Professional <div>&nbsp;What makes Texas State unique is the people who work here. Texas State University seeks candidates whose professional background includes embracing a diversity of people and ideas, a spirit of inclusiveness, a global perspective, and a commitment to community-building.</div> Human Resources <div>&nbsp;What makes Texas State unique is the people who work here. Texas State University seeks candidates whose professional background includes embracing a diversity of people and ideas, a spirit of inclusiveness, a global perspective, and a commitment to community-building.</div> <div>Professional occupations are those that require specialized and theoretical knowledge which is usually acquired through college training or through work experience and other training which provides comparable knowledge. Professional occupations include Personnel and labor relations workers, social workers, doctors, psychologists, registered nurses, economists, dieticians, lawyers, systems analysts, accountants, engineers, employment and vocational rehabilitation counselors, teachers or instructors, police and fire captains, and lieutenants, librarians, management analysts, airplane pilots and navigators, and kindred workers.<br><br>Texas State Professional title examples: Programmer Analyst; Accountant II; Nurse, RN</div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/56216 2026-03-02T08:38:22-06:00 2026-03-02T08:38:22-06:00 Temporary Positions - Administrative Support <div>What really makes Texas State unique is the people who work here. Texas State University seeks candidates whose professional background includes embracing cooperation and ideas, a global perspective, and a commitment to community-building.</div> Human Resources <div>What really makes Texas State unique is the people who work here. Texas State University seeks candidates whose professional background includes embracing cooperation and ideas, a global perspective, and a commitment to community-building.</div> <div>Administrative support employees are responsible for internal and external communication, recording and retrieval of data and/or information, and other paperwork required in an office. Administrative support occupations include bookkeepers, messengers, clerk-typists, stenographers, court transcribers, hearing reporters, statistical clerks, dispatchers, license distributors, payroll clerks, office machine and computer operators, legal assistants, sales workers, cashiers, toll collectors, and kindred workers.<br><br>Texas State administrative support title examples: Payroll Services Asst; Accounting Clerk; Administrative Assistant</div> https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/55998 2026-02-10T14:48:32-06:00 2026-02-10T14:48:33-06:00 Construction Manager II <div>Responsible for planning, designing, estimating, scheduling, directing, and inspecting small to intermediate-sized renovation and construction projects to ensure objectives are met.</div> Facilities Planning Design <ul><li>This position is responsible for planning, designing, estimating, scheduling, directing, and inspecting small to intermediate-sized renovation and construction projects to ensure objectives are met.</li><li>Must have knowledge of: Construction trade standards, codes, regulations, and laws; university standards and construction materials; designing and CADD software; engineering practices and principles and mechanical theory; electrical theory; building trades practices planning, estimating, drafting, and inspection; advanced math; ADA and Life Safety regulations, codes, and statutes.</li><li>Must be skilled in: interacting with interpreting requests from a wide variety of clients, directing the work of others, work as a team member/leader, and negotiating personnel challenges; prioritizing workload; problem solving and decision making.</li><li>Must have the ability to: Read and interpret contract documents, technical manuals, complex schematics, blueprints and other instructions; identify poor workmanship; prepare clear, concise, grammatically accurate documentation and correspondence; assess renovation and major maintenance project scope.</li></ul> <ul><li>Bachelor of Science (BS) with a Major in Construction Science and Management and/or a Certificate in Construction Project Management.</li></ul> <div>Responsible for planning, designing, estimating, scheduling, directing, and inspecting small to intermediate-sized renovation and construction projects to ensure objectives are met.</div> <ul><li>Manage, monitor, and direct contracts with contractors, architects, engineers, consultants for assigned projects.</li><li>Plan, design, schedule, and estimate various requests for new construction projects, facility modification/renovation or major maintenance.</li><li>Develop specifications for goods and services by researching vendor data and referencing applicable codes, regulations and standards.</li><li>Prepare project contract documents including contract change orders and addendums.</li><li>Meet with project requesters, interpret requests for feasibility, and prioritize projects.</li><li>Assist in developing various reports, plans, budgets, and schedules.</li><li>Keep projects current in FPDC.</li><li>Prepare plan review documents.</li><li>Coordinate activities of contractors and physical plant labor and resources to support projects.</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned.</li></ul>"
