      "title": "Job Opportunities",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Home Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student An error occurred while accessing the database. Welcome to the Most Beautiful Campus in Texas What really makes Texas State University unique are the people who work here. We aspire to be an employer of choice with an engaged community that is welcoming to all. Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. New Users Use the site navigation to search for jobs. You must create an account before applying. Returning Users Log in with your username and password to: Edit your existing application Apply to new jobs without re-entering information Review the status of positions you've applied to Current University Employee Users Log in with your Texas State NETID and password to: Create a new application Apply to jobs Review the status of positions you have applied to Contact If you need assistance with the staff or faculty hiring process, to contact a veteran liaison, or for accommodations, please contact Talent Acquisition at talent@txstate.edu . Staff Faculty Volunteer Benefits About Texas State History and Traditions Research Benefits & Perks Texas State’s Annual Security Reports and Fire Safety Report We value the safety of all members of the Texas State University community at our main campus in San Marcos, TX and separate campuses in Maxwell, TX (ALERRT Campus) and Round Rock, TX. Texas State publishes a combined Annual Security and Fire Safety Report that contains information regarding campus safety and security including topics such as: campus law enforcement authority; crime reporting policies; campus alerts (Timely Warnings and Emergency Notifications); fire safety policies and procedures; programs to prevent dating violence, domestic violence, sexual assault and stalking; the procedures the University will follow when one of these crimes is reported; and other matters of importance related to security on campus. The report also contains information about crime statistics for the three most recent calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in on-campus student housing facilities; in noncampus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University or a recognized student organization; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also provides fire statistics for any fires occurring in an on-campus student housing facility during the three most recent calendar years. The Fire Safety Report section and on-campus student housing statistics do not apply to Round Rock or the ALERRT Center, as those campuses do not currently have any student housing facilities. A paper copy of the report is available at Institutional Compliance and Ethics located at Elliott Hall A (201 Talbot Street, San Marcos, TX 78666), by calling (512) 245-4961, or by emailing cleryreport@txstate.edu. Additionally, a PDF of the report can be accessed electronically at www.clery.txstate.edu/report . Accessibility Statement Texas State is committed to maintaining an accessible campus community and providing reasonable accommodations to qualified students, faculty, staff and visitors, including making its web sites accessible. Information related to reasonable accommodation requests can be found on the ADA Compliance website . The digital accessibility statement can also be found online.\r\n. Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
