    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58388": {
      "title": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant NCAA Certification Officer",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant NCAA Certification Officer Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant NCAA Certification Officer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2026771 Posting/Functional Title Assistant NCAA Certification Officer University Pay Plan Title Ast NCAA Certification Officer Location San Marcos Department Athletic Certification Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Full-Time Funding Source Permanent Monthly Salary $3,662.31 Job Category Non-Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. Experience independently researching materials to compile, develop and summarize for professional reports on a frequent or recurring basis. Experience analyzing information, identifying problems, defining alternatives, and developing recommendations for administrators. Experience interpreting and applying rules, regulations, and laws regarding student records. Evidence of the ability to work independently and as a team member. Documented experience communicating orally and in writing with varied stakeholders. High School Diploma. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree Documented experience working with NCAA regulations (Bylaw 14) related to athletic academic eligibility. Experience in evaluating and interpreting degree plans and curriculum, preferably utilizing Degree Works degree audit system. Experience working in the Banner Student Information System environment. Experience working with the NCAA Eligibility Center website and NCAA Academic Portal. Experience working with Teamworks. Knowledge of Texas State’s undergraduate core curriculum and degree program requirements. Job Description The Assistant NCAA Athletics Certification Officer is responsible for assisting the NCAA Athletics Certification Officer in obtaining, evaluating, and documenting the academic credentials in accordance with National Collegiate Athletics Association ( NCAA ) and conference eligibility rules for approximately 400+ student-athletes. Job Duties Eligibility Worksheets – Update and monitor individual SA eligibility worksheets and team eligibility worksheets on a continuous basis. Provide feedback and projections regarding NCAA eligibility to Athletics Academic Center in a timely manner. Certify Student-Athletes for Competition – Review the academic credentials for each SA to determine eligibility status. Assimilate and file appropriate documentation to support certification (i.e. NCAA SA Details Report, transcripts, degree audits, academic progress forms, etc.). Create EDF and submit to Athletics Compliance Office. Academic Pre-Evaluations – Conduct an academic pre-evaluations for prospective student-athletes and provide accurate and timely feedback to the Athletics Compliance Office. Academic Performance Program – Assist the NCAA Certification Officer in updating Compliance Assistant 2.0 with pertinent information for the APP (including APR and GSR ) each year. Work cooperatively with Athletics Academic Center staff and the Athletics Compliance staff to ensure information is accurate. Provide feedback for any NCAA responses to information. Academic Progress Forms – Create, distribute, review, compile and file the academic progress forms from the College Advising centers. Follow up with each College Advising center in a timely manner for clarification when needed. Full-Time Enrollment Monitoring – Oversee the monitoring of full-time enrollment of SAs, managers, male practice players and graduate assistants. Other Assigned Duties – Assist the NCAA Athletic Compliance Officer with general office organization and support. Professionalism – Appearance, attendance, punctuality, and office decorum met Registrar’s office and University policies consistently. Additional Information to Applicants Job Open Date 09/04/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) Open Until Filled Yes Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 8:00AM Normal Work Hours End 5:00PM Posting Notices Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58322 Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have experience conducting an academic pre-evaluation for prospective student athletes? Yes No * Do you have experience with creating, distributing, reviewing, and compiling the file on academic progress forms from the College Advising centers. Follow up with each College Advising center in a timely manner for clarification when needed. Yes No Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
