    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58332": {
      "title": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Education Mobility Outreach Coordinator",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Education Mobility Outreach Coordinator Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Education Mobility Outreach Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2026764 Posting/Functional Title Education Mobility Outreach Coordinator University Pay Plan Title Coord, Education Mobility Location San Marcos Department International Affairs Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Full-Time Funding Source Permanent Monthly Salary $3,750.00 Job Category Non-Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. Bachelor’s degree in communications, marketing, higher education, student affairs, international studies, or related field. Experience with event planning, outreach, recruitment, communications, or student engagement. Excellent interpersonal skills in order to communicate effectively with students, faculty, staff, and community members in 1:1 or presentation style. Must be a U.S. citizen to hold certification with the U.S. Department of State as a Passport Facility Agent. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in higher education or student services. Experience with international education, study abroad, domestic exchange or student travel, or student mobility programming. Experience presenting to groups and coordinating campus events. Familiarity with Canva, Adobe Creative Suite, social media analytics, or CRM /student engagement platforms. Job Description The Education Mobility Outreach Coordinator is responsible for providing outreach and recruitment efforts for the three Education Mobility units to increase student enrollment and drive awareness of programs. This position reports directly to the Director of Education Mobility. Job Duties Assist in developing strategies to increase student awareness and participation in Education Abroad and Study in America programs. Represent Education Mobility at tabling events, student organization fairs, orientations, classroom presentations, campus events, and community outreach opportunities. Conduct presentations and information sessions for students and campus partners. Including, but not limited to, attending New Student Orientations. Coordinate logistics and promotional efforts for Education Mobility events, including but not limited to: Education Abroad/Study in America fair, pre-departure orientations, workshops, recruitment events, passport office programing and educational workshops, etc. Coordinating logistics includes assisting with scheduling, room reservations, event set up, event communications, event materials, promotional signage, etc. Could also include attending evening and occasional weekend events as needed. Administratively maintain outreach calendars, outreach metrics, event attendance, and recruitment outcomes having data ready to provide when requested. Keep up with all inventory of marketing and recruitment materials, requesting an order of new supplies, as needed, including program T-Shirts. Manage Education Mobility social media accounts and assist in developing engaging promotional content. Includes responding to social media messages, inquiries, and outreach communications in a professional and timely manner. Create graphics, flyers, digital signage, promotional materials, and marketing campaigns for events and programs. Includes coordinating the distribution of marketing materials across campus and within the surrounding community. Create, maintain, and update Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) for outreach activities, recruitment processes, and systems utilized by Education Abroad and Study in America. Support passport office walk-in days directing the customer flow. Additional Information to Applicants Job Open Date 08/28/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) 09/07/2026 Open Until Filled No Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 8:00AM Normal Work Hours End 5:00PM Posting Notices Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58273 Applicant Document Required Documents Resume List of References Optional Documents Cover Letter Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
