    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58307": {
      "title": "Job Opportunities",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Senior Network Administrator Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Senior Network Administrator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Limited hybrid work may be available after onboarding, typically up to one day per week, subject to operational needs and supervisor approval. This position is eligible for hybrid or remote work opportunities, subject to university policy and departmental needs. ITAC will not sponsor or transfer visa sponsorship for this position. Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2026754 Posting/Functional Title Senior Network Administrator University Pay Plan Title Sr Network Administrator Location San Marcos Department Network Operations Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Full-Time Funding Source Permanent Monthly Salary Commensurate with experience Job Category Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. Five years of professional experience in network administration, network engineering, or closely related enterprise network infrastructure work. Professional experience administering enterprise routing and switching infrastructure in a production environment. Professional experience with dynamic routing protocols, such as BGP , OSPF , IS-IS, or EIGRP . Professional experience supporting enterprise wireless networking technologies. Professional experience supporting network security technologies, such as firewalls, IPS / IDS , network access control, Cisco ISE , segmentation, or related security platforms. Preferred Qualifications Experience supporting data center network infrastructure. Experience with network fabric technologies, such as EVPN / VXLAN , Cisco SDA , ACI , virtualized routing, or comparable fabric-based architectures. Experience supporting MPLS , VRF , SD- WAN , or complex WAN routing environments. Experience with Cisco ISE , NAC , 802.1X, device profiling, guest access, posture, or network segmentation. Experience with network automation using Python, Ansible, APIs, Git, configuration management systems, or similar tools. Experience working in higher education, government, large enterprise, healthcare, or another complex multi-site environment. Current or prior network-related certifications, such as CCNP , CCIE , JNCIP , CWNP , Aruba, Ruckus, Fortinet, Palo Alto, or comparable credentials. Job Description Texas State University is hiring a Sr. Network Administrator to help design, operate, secure, and modernize the university’s multi-campus network infrastructure. This is a senior technical role responsible for supporting enterprise wired, wireless, data center, security, and wide-area network services used across the university. The position works with a broad range of network technologies, including routing and switching, network fabrics, data center networks, wireless infrastructure, SD- WAN , network security platforms, Cisco ISE , monitoring systems, and automation tools. The successful candidate will be expected to provide technical leadership, solve complex problems, contribute to network architecture decisions, and help deliver infrastructure projects from planning through implementation. About the Job Texas State University operates a large, heterogeneous network environment supporting academic, administrative, residential, research, and campus life services. The network includes equipment and platforms from multiple manufacturers, including Cisco, Juniper, HP/Aruba, and Ruckus Wireless. The team emphasizes reliable service delivery, standards-based design, operational consistency, security, documentation, and continuous improvement. This role will have meaningful technical ownership in the operation and evolution of the campus network. Responsibilities include both hands-on administration and higher-level engineering work, such as developing standards, improving network reliability, leading technical projects, mentoring other staff, and coordinating with vendors and campus stakeholders. Job Duties Design, administer, maintain, and troubleshoot enterprise network infrastructure, including campus routing and switching, wireless, data center networks, network fabrics, WAN /SD- WAN , and related services. Support network security and access control platforms, including Cisco ISE , network segmentation, authentication/authorization policies, and related security integrations. Diagnose and resolve complex network incidents affecting wired, wireless, data center, WAN , and security services. Lead and support network infrastructure projects from planning through implementation, including design, change coordination, testing, documentation, and operational handoff. Develop and maintain network standards, diagrams, procedures, configuration templates, and operational documentation. Monitor network performance, availability, capacity, and reliability; identify trends and recommend improvements. Automate network operations using scripting, APIs, configuration management tools, monitoring platforms, and AI-assisted workflows where appropriate. Provide technical leadership, mentorship, and vendor coordination; participate in a shared after-hours on-call rotation, currently one week every six weeks. Additional Information to Applicants Limited hybrid work may be available after onboarding, typically up to one day per week, subject to operational needs and supervisor approval. This position is eligible for hybrid or remote work opportunities, subject to university policy and departmental needs. ITAC will not sponsor or transfer visa sponsorship for this position. Job Open Date 08/26/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) Open Until Filled Yes Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 8:00AM Normal Work Hours End 5:00PM Posting Notices Applicant must have a valid Texas Driver's License and be a driver in good standing with less than ten (10) points deducted for driving infractions as determined by the employer driving standards system. Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58218 Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Describe your day-to-day duties during your most recent five years of professional experience as a Network Administrator, Network Engineer, or equivalent enterprise network infrastructure role. Your response should clearly identify the network technologies, platforms, and responsibilities you worked with directly. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your professional experience designing, administering, or troubleshooting enterprise routing, WAN, or network fabric technologies. Your response should identify the protocols, technologies, platforms, and environments you have worked with directly, such as BGP, OSPF, IS-IS, EIGRP, MPLS, VRF, SD-WAN, EVPN/VXLAN, Cisco SDA, ACI, or similar technologies. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your professional experience administering, supporting, or troubleshooting enterprise network security and access control technologies. Your response should identify the platforms, tools, and responsibilities you have worked with directly, such as Cisco ISE, NAC, 802.1X, MAB, RADIUS/TACACS+, network segmentation, firewall policy, IPS/IDS, VPN, secure network design, or similar technologies. (Open Ended Question) * Will you be able to perform all the physical requirements of the assigned duties, such as moving around the university? Yes No * Will you be able to work in-office at the San Marcos campus 5 days a week, Monday - Friday, 8:00AM - 5:00PM Yes No Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
