    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58266": {
      "title": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | GIS Technician",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | GIS Technician Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student GIS Technician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2026748 Posting/Functional Title GIS Technician University Pay Plan Title Grant Specialist Location Other - Fort Knox, Kentucky Department Center for Archaeological Studies Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Full-Time Funding Source Grant Monthly Salary Commensurate with Experience Job Category Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. Successful completion of a four-year undergraduate degree in geography, GIS , an environmental discipline or related field from an accredited university or a GIS certificate from an accredited university. A combination of education and experience may be used in lieu of an accredited four-year undergraduate degree or certificate. Demonstrated knowledge of ArcGIS Pro and Online or QGIS and associated mobile mapping products. Demonstrated ability to develop and manage GIS data and databases. Experience in using Microsoft Word, Excel, and databases for the development of supporting environmental analysis. Ability to communicate effectively in formal briefings and in general public meetings, and to prepare clear and concise written materials appropriate for different audiences. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge and use of Army GIS specifications. Knowledge of relevant environmental, natural, and cultural resources processes at military installations and the integration with other environmental laws. Ability to gather facts, analyze and compare trends, draw conclusions, devise solutions to problems, and identify changes and trends related to comprehensive planning issues. Candidate must be able to work independently as well as part of a team that regularly interacts with military and civilian personnel and state and federal agencies. Job Description Texas State University is searching for a GIS Technician who can support the environmental compliance program at Fort Knox, located near Louisville, Kentucky. We are looking for a person who can provide technical guidance to the Government in performing data acquisition and analysis that is accurate, complete, current, and valid for the installation’s environmental layers. This includes coordinating with the government regarding implementation of the GIS program; strategic planning; compliance with federal, state, local, and Army Regulations, Directives, and Standards; providing technical support to the Government in the development of Standard Operating Procedures and management plans. This may also include providing technical input and recommendations regarding GIS operations, capabilities, and collection of data. This position is located at Fort Knox, Kentucky, which is located just south of Louisville, Kentucky. Louisville is the largest city in Kentucky and is a cultural, entertainment, and sporting hub for the area. The primary objective of this position is to provide scientific and technical skills pertaining to the implementation of the Fort Knox air program. The job will involve a wide range of natural resource and environmental compliance projects that support military training and development. Job Duties GIS Data Development and Maintenance Gather, update, maintain, and/or access all existing GIS data including: Planimetric, utility, operations and security, master planning, environmental, cultural resources, and natural resources using the most recently available aerial photography, GPS field data collection and validation, hard-copy maps, as-built drawings, data conversion, and in-house knowledge. Providing technical input to the Government in determining the most appropriate GIS workflow procedures including data format, storage, and maintenance. It may require projecting geographically un-projected data layers provided by outside entities such as the surrounding local governments and/or State or Federally available data. Continue to develop, maintain, and make available metadata for all geospatial data maintained in the GIS database. This effort will provide another level of credibility to Ft Knox GIS data. Current data layers to be updated on an annual basis: 41 Compliance layers and 12 Conservation layers. Provide customized geodatabases that are created, implemented and supported within ESRI ArcGIS to meet the varied needs of installation staff and to support external units, agencies, and activities. All geospatial data layer creation and updates shall conform to the established guidelines; be capable of being incorporated into the Installation GIS programs; comply with applicable security requirements; comply with the latest SDSFIE version, FGDC standards, & IGI &S guidelines to include current Quality Assurance Plans (QAP’s). GIS Mapping and Analysis Support Provide mapping and GIS analysis support to the Government. This includes: specialized GIS analysis including project specific GIS and/or GIS related data; specialized GIS analysis support, including interpretation and analysis of environmental data and development of natural resource support recommendations; and support to planning and siting studies, and environmental impact assessments. Implement consistency of design across all GIS mapping products, including the utilization of standard symbology on mapping products, to sustain consistency with Federal agencies, DoD organizations. GPS Support and Validation. Provide GPS field data collection and validation support. Field data collection will be coordinated with the Government Tech Rep. Data collected will be post-processed, as needed, by the Partner prior to integration with the GIS . If required, participate in meetings with agencies in support of GPS - related activities. Additional Information to Applicants Job Open Date 08/24/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) 09/06/2026 Open Until Filled No Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 8:00AM Normal Work Hours End 5:00PM Posting Notices Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58238 Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
