    "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58210": {
      "title": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Senior Proposal Coordinator",
      "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Senior Proposal Coordinator Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Senior Proposal Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Posting Number 2026734 Posting/Functional Title Senior Proposal Coordinator University Pay Plan Title Sr Proposal Coordinator Location Other - Hybrid Department Pre-Award Sponsored Programs Recruitment Type Open Recruiting Job Type Full-Time Funding Source Permanent Monthly Salary $5,416.67 Job Category Exempt Required Qualifications: Applicants must specifically address how they meet these required qualifications to meet the requirements of the position. At least two years of experience in proposal review, including budgets. Knowledge of applicable federal and state regulations—including compliance areas (effort, human subjects, export control, national security)—and various funding source requirements (such as NIH , NSF , DOE , DoD, USDA / NIFA , foundation, and industry sponsors), and ability to interpret and explain complex regulations. Familiarity with electronic submission portals (e.g., Grants.gov, E-Grants, Tex-grants, Research.gov). Demonstrated communication, customer service, conflict resolution, teamwork, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to navigate challenging situations professionally. Demonstrated ability to manage complex projects involving multiple stakeholders, competing priorities, and strict deadlines. Bachelor’s degree Preferred Qualifications Certified Research Administrator ( CRA ), Certified Pre-Award Research Administrator ( CPRA ), or willingness to achieve certification. Experience with Kuali, Cayuse, SAP , Workday or other finance or research administration software . At least four years of research administration or sponsored programs experience, particularly in a university setting. Advanced Excel skills, Planner, Power Automate, or AI tools. Knowledge of university policies and procedures. Job Description Senior Proposal Coordinator is responsible for coordinating all aspects of compliance verification, review, and submission of grant proposals as well as conducting the final institutional review and clearance. Job Duties Senior Proposal Coordinator The Senior Proposal Coordinator serves as the institutional review authority for sponsored proposals and is responsible for coordinating proposal review, compliance verification, and submission activities in accordance with university policies and sponsor requirements. Proposal Review & Submission Review, coordinate, and submit grant proposals and related documents for federal, state, foundation, and other sponsors. Conduct final institutional review to ensure proposals are complete, accurate, and compliant with sponsor requirements and university policies. Verify required approvals, certifications, budgets, and supporting documentation prior to submission. Proposal Coordination & Project Management Monitor proposal pipelines, deadlines, and submission activities. Work closely with Research Coordinators, faculty, and administrative staff to facilitate timely proposal preparation and submission. Identify issues that may affect submission timelines and assist in resolving them. Compliance & Risk Review Ensure adherence to sponsor guidelines, university policies, and applicable regulations. Review budgets, cost sharing, F&A rates, subrecipient documentation, and other proposal components for compliance. Escalate complex compliance or policy issues to appropriate offices and leadership. Sponsor & Institutional Liaison Support Communicate with sponsors, collaborating institutions, and internal stakeholders regarding proposal requirements, submission processes, and administrative matters. Coordinate with other university offices as needed to support proposal development and review. Customer Service & Communication Provide responsive support and guidance to faculty, staff, and colleagues regarding proposal preparation, sponsor requirements, and submission procedures. Promote collaborative working relationships and a high level of customer service. Training & Operational Support Assist with updating procedures, forms, and guidance materials. Support onboarding, mentoring, and training of new staff. Contribute to special projects, reporting activities, and continuous improvement efforts within the office. Additional Information to Applicants Job Open Date 08/14/2026 Job Close Date (posting closes at midnight) Open Until Filled Yes Normal Work Days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Normal Work Hours Start 8:00AM Normal Work Hours End 5:00PM Posting Notices Legal and Required Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Choose Texas State University? Join the Texas State Bobcat team and experience a career that offers more than just a job—it’s a path to a brighter future. As a Texas State employee, you’ll enjoy: Exceptional Benefits: Comprehensive health insurance with 100% premium coverage for employees and 50% for dependents, starting on your first day. Generous Time Off: Enjoy vacation, holidays, sick leave, and more to maintain a healthy work-life balance. Wellness and Balance: Access a FREE wellness program, plus mother and family-friendly resources to support your personal well-being. Professional Growth: Explore a wide range of training, development courses, certifications, and educational support programs. Welcoming Campus: Become part of a vibrant Bobcat community with numerous social and professional networks. Tuition Benefits: Take advantage of tuition support for yourself and for your dependent children, making higher education more accessible for your family. Retirement Security: Secure your future with TRS pension, retirement plans, and voluntary savings options with strong employer contributions. At Texas State University, you’re not just an employee—you’re a valued member of a thriving and beautiful campus community. Start your journey with us today. https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57656 Applicant Document Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
